    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank-faculty-position--Basic-Pharmaceutical-Sciences---Promotion-Path_R0006591": {
      "title": "Open Rank faculty position, Basic Pharmaceutical Sciences – Promotion Path",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Department of Basic Pharmaceutical Sciences in the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy at High Point University invites applications for a full-time, 12-month promotion path (non-tenure track) faculty position. The individual in this position will be primarily responsible for teaching PharmD students but will also be expected to contribute to new knowledge through scholarship and provide service to the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy, the University, and the greater High Point community. The estimated distribution of effort for this individual at program maturity (i.e., when a full faculty cohort is hired) will be 60-70% teaching, 20-30% service, and 10-15% scholarship. Academic rank will be commensurate with experience. Applicants with areas of expertise/interest within the broad discipline of pharmaceutical sciences are welcome to apply. Areas of priority include physiology or pharmacology. Instructional duties may include both lecture or laboratory settings. Interested candidates should apply by submitting the following documents as a single PDF file: • Cover letter describing your professional goals, relevant academic preparation, and experience • Current curriculum vitae • Statement of teaching/mentoring philosophy (one page) • Statement of scholarship interests and philosophy (one page) • Contact information for two professional references For additional information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Kent Stewart, Interim Chair and Associate Professor of Basic Pharmaceutical Sciences at kstewar1@highpoint.edu. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Pharm.D., M.D., or Ph.D. in pharmacology, physiology, toxicology, biochemistry, or related biomedical science field is required Experience and Training: Postdoctoral experience and strong academic credentials in areas of relevance to pharmacy, such as pharmacology or biochemistry is strongly preferred. Medical or pharmacy academic teaching experience is strongly preferred, and priority will be given to candidates with prior teaching experience in one of these settings. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Strong verbal and written communication skills are required Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others is required ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Develop, coordinate, and teach content within the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy integrated curriculum as appointed by the Department Chair. Develop and offer an elective course that corresponds with expertise area(s) as needed. Utilize ExamSoft® or other software to conduct all School of Pharmacy assessments. Provide mentorship and advisement for students in the School of Pharmacy as appointed by the Dean’s Office and Department Chair. Communicate teaching and scholarship activities through frequent and effective communication with the Department Chair . Contribute to new knowledge through scholarship in the individual’s field of study or Scholarship of Teaching & Learning (SoTL). Integrate and enhance collaborations among the clinical sciences and basic sciences in areas of scholarship, education, and service. Advance the service missions of the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy and High Point University to meet community needs. Act as a representative and advocate for the department, the school of pharmacy and the University. Actively participate in committees within the Department, School of Pharmacy, and University and participate in professional and governmental organizations as appointed by the Department Chair. Abide by University and School of Pharmacy policies. Undertake other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Chair of Basic Pharmaceutical Sciences. ACCOUNTABILITY: Excellence in teaching, scholarship and service For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Samson Amos, Chair, Department of Basic Pharmaceutical Sciences, at samos@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Basic-Pharmaceutical-Sciences-and-Director-of-Research----Tenured-Tenure-Track-or-Promotion-Path_R0006268": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Basic Pharmaceutical Sciences – Promotion Path",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Department of Basic Pharmaceutical Sciences in the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy at High Point University invites applications for a full-time, 12-month promotion path (non-tenure track) faculty position. The individual in this position will be primarily responsible for teaching PharmD students but will also be expected to contribute to new knowledge through scholarship and provide service to the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy, the University, and the greater High Point community. The estimated distribution of effort for this individual at program maturity (i.e., when a full faculty cohort is hired) will be 60-80% teaching, 10-30% service, and 10-15% scholarship. Academic rank will be commensurate with experience. Applicants with areas of expertise/interest within the broad discipline of pharmaceutical sciences are welcome to apply. Candidates with experience in drug development areas, such as Medicinal Chemistry, Pharmacology, Physiology, pharmaceutics, manufacturing, compounding, or pharmacokinetics/pharmacodynamics, are particularly encouraged to apply. Instructional duties may include both lecture and laboratory settings. Interested candidates should apply by submitting the following documents as a single PDF file: • Cover letter describing your professional goals, relevant academic preparation, and experience • Current curriculum vitae • Statement of teaching/mentoring philosophy (one page) • Statement of scholarship interests and philosophy (one page) • Contact information for two professional references QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Pharm.D., M.D., or Ph.D. in pharmaceutics, pharmacology, physiology, toxicology, medicinal chemistry, biochemistry, or related biomedical science field is required Experience and Training: Postdoctoral experience and strong academic credentials in areas of relevance to pharmacy, such as pharmaceutics, pharmacology, biochemistry or related biomedical science field is strongly preferred. Medical or pharmacy academic teaching experience is strongly preferred, and priority will be given to candidates with prior teaching experience in one of these settings. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Strong verbal and written communication skills are required Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others is required ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Develop, coordinate, and teach content within the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy integrated curriculum as appointed by the Department Chair. Develop and offer an elective course that corresponds with expertise area(s) as needed. Utilize ExamSoft® or other software to conduct all School of Pharmacy assessments. Provide mentorship and advisement for students in the School of Pharmacy as appointed by the Dean’s Office and Department Chair. Communicate teaching and scholarship activities through frequent and effective communication with the Department Chair . Contribute to new knowledge through scholarship in the individual’s field of study or Scholarship of Teaching & Learning (SoTL). Integrate and enhance collaborations among the clinical sciences and basic sciences in areas of scholarship, education, and service. Advance the service missions of the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy and High Point University to meet community needs. Act as a representative and advocate for the department, the school of pharmacy and the University. Actively participate in admissions interviews and committees within the Department, School of Pharmacy, and University. Participate in professional and governmental organizations as approved by the Department Chair. Abide by University and School of Pharmacy policies. Undertake other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Chair of Basic Pharmaceutical Sciences. ACCOUNTABILITY: Excellence in teaching, scholarship and service For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Samson Amos, Chair, Department of Basic Pharmaceutical Sciences at samos@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Nursing-Simulation-Director--Open-Rank-Faculty-Position_R0007767-1": {
      "title": "Nursing Simulation Director, Open Rank Faculty Position",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Teresa B. Caine School of Nursing at High Point University seeks a full-time faculty member to serve as our Simulation Director. The ideal candidate will have evidence-based teaching skills and clinical expertise to support student success across the pre-licensure BSN curriculum. This position requires flexibility for evening and weekend instruction, direct clinical supervision as needed, and participation in service activities. The Simulation Director is responsible for leading and managing all aspects of the simulation program within the School of Nursing. This role involves developing, implementing, and evaluating simulation experiences that enhance learning outcomes and simultaneously prepare students for success in nursing practice. Expertise in nursing education, simulation technology, and program management is required. Leading or co-facilitating students’ learning in adult health (medical-surgical) nursing courses and foundational support courses under the nursing dean's guidance are also requirements. Knowledge of adult pedagogical principles, and a commitment to excellence in nursing education and student success are essential. Qualifications Education: Minimum- Master’s degree in nursing education or equivalent from an accredited institution Preferred - Doctorate degree in nursing or equivalent from an accredited institution Experience: Three or more years of clinical expertise as an RN in adult health (medical-surgical) Three or more years of nursing education experience (classroom and clinical) in a BSN educational program (at minimum) Previous experience as a simulation educator, using standardized patients and patient simulators Certification in Healthcare Simulation (CHSE) or other formal simulation training Licensure: •      Unrestricted license as a Registered Nurse in North Carolina (or eligible) Faculty Responsibilities Clinical practicum supervision, clinical skills laboratory instruction, simulation-based learning facilitation, classroom teaching using evidence-based methodology Development of course assessments aligned with Next Generation NCLEX-RN standards Participation in university and departmental service activities, student recruitment, academic advising, scholarship or creative works, and mentorship of current and prospective students Maintain classrooms, nursing clinical skills lab, simulation suites (including inventory), etc. Design evidence-based simulation scenarios that align with learning objectives and competency requirements Mentor nursing faculty to integrate simulation pedagogy, debriefing techniques, and the delivery of “best practice” and “evidence-based practice” into respective courses Oversee the selection, procurement, and maintenance of simulation equipment and technology Manage relationships with equipment vendors and technical support services Maintain detailed records of simulation activities, outcomes, and assessments Lead strategic planning initiatives for continuous improvement of simulation-based learning experiences, program enhancement, and expansion Maintain simulation program scheduling, resource allocation, policies, procedures, and standards in alignment with regulatory and accreditation requirements Additional duties as assigned Essential Knowledge Familiarity with North Carolina Board of Nursing’s regulations and standards Familiarity with accreditation standards (CCNE preferred), adult education principles, and standards for professional nursing practice (BSN education level) Familiarity with NCLEX-RN Test Plan and Next Generation NCLEX Knowledge of simulation center design and operations with a commitment to continuous quality improvement Essential Skills A record of scholarship to meet the desired academic rank (i.e., instructor, assistant professor, or associate professor) Technology skills with proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, database management, and high-fidelity simulation equipment and software CPR certified Exceptional organizational, interpersonal, collaborative, team building, and effective communication skills orally, in writing, and through technology Student-centered Commitment to multiculturalism in all settings Experience with learning management systems and educational technology Expertise in simulation pedagogy and adult learning principles Strong leadership, organization, project management, and time-management skills Ability To Work independently and manage multiple priorities Lift and move simulation equipment up to fifty pounds with prolonged standing and walking Track inventory (skills lab and simulation equipment) Follow instructions as well as take initiatives Adapt to change in a progressive environment of constant change Embrace working in an interdisciplinary atmosphere Lead clinical instruction at practicum sites For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Racquel Ingram, Founding Dean, School of Nursing at ringram1@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank--Non-tenure--Optometric-Faculty-Position_R0007513": {
      "title": "Open Rank, Non-tenure, Optometric Faculty Position",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-10-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHigh Point University's School of Optometry is seeking to appoint a group of optometric faculty members with specialties in foundational sciences, ocular disease, primary care, contact lenses, pediatrics, binocular vision, and vision rehabilitation. The ideal candidates will be passionate about educating the next generation of optometrists, engaging in scholarly activities, and contributing to the advancement of the optometric profession. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Earned doctoral level degree (O.D., Ph.D., or equivalent) degree from an accredited optometry school in a discipline related to the mission of the School of Optometry. Experience and Training: Minimum of three years clinical experience in optometry or completion of an optometric residency. Experience in academic settings as an instructor or researcher is highly desirable. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Strong foundation in optometric care and its various subspecialties. Ability to engage and inspire students. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Commitment to research and scholarly activity. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Provide high-quality instruction in optometry courses, including lectures, labs, and clinical supervision. Develop and maintain a research program, with a focus on contributing to the body of knowledge in optometric science and practice. Engage in service activities within the School of Optometry, the university, and the broader professional community. Advise and mentor optometry students in academic, research, and clinical capacities. Collaborate with faculty members across departments to enhance interdisciplinary learning. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Paula Luke, Professor and Associate Dean of Academics, School of Optometry at pluke@highpoint.edu . As part of the hiring process, the HPU School of Optometry may obtain a consumer report from the National Student Clearinghouse to verify educational credentials for employment purposes."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Sales_R0007073": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Sales",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-11-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Congdon School of Entrepreneurship at High Point University is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Sales. We are looking to fill sections of Sales courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Mr. Laurence Quinn, Chair of the Department of Sales at lquinn@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: MBA in the teaching discipline preferred; and appropriate professional experience in the teaching discipline will be considered. Upload an unofficial copy of your Masters transcript.  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  This will be used to verify you have at least 18 graduate semester hours in an appropriate subject. Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). If you have less than 18 hours, we will consider your commensurate experience/training.  Be sure this is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Sports-Announcing-Practicum_R0009050": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Sports Announcing Practicum",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nThe Nido R. Qubein School of Communication is seeking a part-time Adjunct Instructor to teach SPT 2269 Sports Announcing Practicum this spring. In this course, students will learn the fundamentals of sports announcing including play-by-play of live sporting events, sports talk shows, sports anchoring, and sports interviewing. Students will learn how to prepare for their announcing assignments by doing research, developing game notes and charts, incorporating anecdotal material, and using statistics and data. Students will also learn announcing techniques such as vocal control, tone, pacing, and the proper care of their voice. Qualifications: Master's degree with 18 hours in the field OR Master's degree with commensurate experience For more information regarding this position, please contact Ken Medlin, Chair of Journalism and Sports Media Department – kmedlin1@highpoint.edu"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Assitant-Professor--Biology_R0009007": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Biology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Department of Biology at High Point University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Biology position with an expected start date of August 2027. This position is a 9-month, non-tenure track position eligible for promotion to Associate and Professor ranks and multi-year contract extensions. Responsibilities include teaching introductory and advanced biology courses with the opportunity to offer interdisciplinary honors and general education courses. Successful candidates will have a demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and experiential learning. The Assistant Professor will also be responsible for developing an active research program involving undergraduate students. Successful candidates will have access to professional development funding. Preference will be given to candidates with teaching and/or research experience in animal physiology, including related fields such as behavioral physiology, comparative physiology, evolutionary physiology, or ecophysiology (including aquatic biology). Ability to teach human physiology, human anatomy, comparative anatomy, and related topics is also highly valued. Candidates with research focuses suitable for implementation at primarily undergraduate institutions including rat models, aquatic models, cellular models, or non-rodent animal models are strongly encouraged to apply. A Ph.D. in biology or a closely related field is required, and post-doctoral experience is preferred. The position includes the use of our state-of-the-art Wanek School of Natural Sciences, which houses the Departments of Biology, Chemistry, Neuroscience and Physics. The Biology Department offers a B.S., a B.A., and minor in biology. Biology courses additionally serve as foundational elements of applied and health science degrees at High Point University. The assistant professor will be responsible for advising biology majors, and for service to the department, school, and university. Applications should include the following items, submitted as a single document: (i) a cover letter addressing the applicant’s qualifications and interest in the position, (ii) curriculum vitae, (iii) a statement of teaching philosophy (including a description of approaches to teaching both science and non-science majors), (iv) a statement of research interests, and (v) an unofficial transcript with the highest awarded degree. Additionally, three letters of recommendation should be provided; letters of recommendation should be emailed by references to Dr. Matthew Talbert ( mtalbert@highpoint.edu ). Review of applications will begin on September 18, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For additional information, please contact Dr. Matthew Talbert, mtalbert@highpoint.edu . High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas.    At High Point University the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information or veteran status and other legally protected statuses. We encourage all applicants to apply."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Department-Chair-and-Open-Rank-Faculty-of-Physics_R0007945": {
      "title": "Department Chair and Open Rank Faculty of Physics, 10 Month",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nThe Department of Physics at High Point University invites applications for a department chair to begin August 2027. This is a 10-month, non-tenure track, open-rank position eligible for multi-year contract extensions and promotion to Associate or Professor ranks. The ideal candidate will be a visionary leader and accomplished scholar who will guide a dynamic and collaborative department committed to excellence and innovation in teaching, research, and service. This role will oversee curriculum and program development, faculty and staff development, research initiatives, and student recruitment and success. The chair will also work collaboratively with other departments and the dean to advance the mission of the Wanek School of Natural Sciences and High Point University. Additionally, the successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate physics across the curriculum, maintain an active research program involving undergraduate students, and contribute to the Department, School, and wider University through service responsibilities. The B.S. Physics program at High Point University values engaging and effective teaching, the integration of computation, experiment, and theory across the curriculum, and undergraduate research (http://www.highpoint.edu/physics/). The program seeks a dynamic individual who will embrace these values and is passionate about mentoring undergraduates and working collaboratively with colleagues. Successful applicants will have access to startup and institutional research and professional development funding, and laboratory and office space in the 128,000-square-foot Wanek School of Natural Sciences, which includes innovative classroom and laboratory spaces and the Culp Planetarium. A Ph.D. in physics or closely related field is required, as is demonstrated leadership experience in an academic setting. QUALIFICATIONS:   Education   Ph.D. in physics   or closely related field   Applications should   inc l u de the following items,   submitted as a   single document : ( i ) a cover letter addressing the applicant’s qualifications and   vision for the department , (ii) curriculum vitae, (iii) a statement of teaching philosophy, (iv) a statement of research interests, and (v) an unofficial transcript with the highest awarded degree. Additionally,   the names and contact information for at least   three   professional references   should be provided.        For   additional   information, please contact Dr. Briana Fiser, Dean of the Wanek School of Natural Sciences, at   bfiser@highpoint.edu .        Apply online at   https://highpoint.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Highpoint-Faculty .   Review of applications will begin October   12th   and continue until the position is filled .   Applicants who do not meet the qualifications or are not legally authorized to work in the US will not be considered.     High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas.      At High Point   University   the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University prohibits discrimination   on the basis of   race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender   identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information or veteran status and other legally protected statuses. We encourage all applicants to apply."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Persuasion-and-Negotiation_R0009016": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Persuasion and Negotiation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Nido R. Qubein School of Communication at High Point University seeks an Adjunct Communication and Business Leadership (CBL) Instructor to teach a course, Persuasion and Negotiation (CBL 5200) starting January 6, 2027. The course description states that business people need analytical skills to discover optimal solutions to problems but need persuasion and negotiation skills to get them implemented. The course asks students to learn persuasion and negotiation skills experientially and to understand communication strategies via analytical and theoretical frameworks. The class emphasizes readings, simulations, exercises, and case study analysis. Successful applicants will be assigned to teach this course as a hybrid online with in-person meetings for High Point University in the upcoming Spring 2026 semester or placed in our adjunct pool for future consideration to teach additional CBL courses. For more information about this position, please contact Dr. Tim Koba, Director of the MA-CBL program, at tkoba@highpoint.edu. Applications received on or before October 1, 2026 will be given priority consideration. Qualifications Required: Education: Preferred an earned doctoral, or terminal degree, in Management, Business, Leadership, or a related field. Master’s degree in Management, Business, Leadership, or a related field, with experience in the topic to be taught. Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Professional experience in negotiation positions is preferred. Essential Functions: Successfully teach Persuasion and Negotiation at the Master’s degree level. Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. These can be done via phone or virtually. Application Materials: Upload an unofficial copy of your educational transcript.  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to provide an official transcript. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Cover letter At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank-Professor-of-Mechanical-Engineering_R0008965": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Webb School of Engineering at High Point University seeks a full-time, open-rank Mechanical Engineering faculty member to teach courses in manufacturing, mechanical design, and vibrations, beginning August 2027. HPU launched new Mechanical Engineering and Mechatronics majors in Fall 2024 and opened a state-of-the-art Makerspace and Machine Shop in Fall 2026. We seek a creative, dynamic individual to play a critical role in the development of innovative, active learning classes and laboratories, and to mentor highly motivated students in undergraduate research projects and design competitions. The successful candidate will teach a variety of courses within the Mechanical Engineering and Mechatronics programs. Additional expectations include academic advising, supporting undergraduate research, assisting the department with ABET accreditation, and serving on college and university-wide committees. Faculty appointments are for a nine-month contract period with a normal teaching load of 12 credit hours per semester. Qualifications Education Candidates must have an earned Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, or a closely related field like Aerospace, Manufacturing, or Materials Science. Industry experience is also desirable. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: The successful candidate should have demonstrated promise of excellence in teaching, a record of scholarly achievement, an entrepreneurial spirit and an interest in working with highly motivated undergraduate students. The success of our undergraduate students is our primary focus. Responsibilities Teach 12 contact hours (typically 2 – 3 classes) per semester Advise and mentor students Produce scholarly research or creative activity, especially in partnership with undergraduate students Assist with curriculum development and ABET Accreditation Assist with university recruiting efforts Participate in department, college, and university meetings and committees Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair and/or Dean Application Materials Applicants should upload the following documents as one combined PDF file . A cover letter A current CV A statement of teaching philosophy A statement of research interests Names and contact information for three professional references Any questions related to this position should be sent to Dr. Brian Bernard, Department Chair of Mechanical Engineering and Mechatronics, bbernard@highpoint.edu . Review of applications will begin September 28th and will continue until the position is filled. Start date is August 2027. Applicants who don’t meet the qualifications or are not legally authorized to work in the US will not be considered. Choose to be Extraordinary!"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Attending-Faculty--Public-Health-Dentist--Clinical-Assistant-Associate-Professor_R0006463": {
      "title": "Attending Faculty, Public Health Dentist, Clinical Assistant/Associate/Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHigh Point University Health, LLC and the affiliated Oral Health Network (OHN) is a not-for-profit oral health system that is part of the Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM), with a mission of putting those who need our care at the center of everything we do. The Attending Dentist, Faculty Clinician (Public Health) is a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure track faculty appointment with duties in the High Point University Oral Health Network (OHN) and Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM), which includes the pre-doctoral Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. The Attending Dentist, Faculty Clinician (Public Health) will support clinical care, community-based oral health initiatives, and learner education. The faculty clinician will help implement and grow an innovative community-based care model through the HPU OHN Mobile Unit, with a focus on expanding access to care for underserved populations in the local High Point community. The role will also include part-time patient care at a local community care clinic and collaboration with internal and external partners to strengthen sustainable community oral health initiatives. QUALIFICATIONS:   DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent) Active dental licensure in the state of North Carolina Experience and Training 3 years of experience in clinical practice of dentistry is preferred, but not required. Experience in dental education is preferred, but not required. Additional knowledge, skills, and abilities preferred for this role include: Robust verbal and written communication skills Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU WSDM’s core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Clinical documentation, diagnosis, and treatment planning using electronic health records (EHR) such as EPIC systems. Adaptability Coachability Integrity and innovation Trustworthy SALARY AND BENEFITS: Eligible candidates may meet criteria for Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) High Point University benefit and perks (employer matched 401K plan, vision, dental, health, tuition waiver for child, disability insurance, life insurance, CE and more). Base salary commensurate with experience and rank. OHN Incentive based on patient care thresholds. ACCOUNTABILITY:   Report to Chief Dental Officer (CDO) Collaborates with other WSDM faculty and community partners to monitor, evaluate, and grow the success of community partnerships Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews are conducted along with an annual assessment by the CDO. These reviews include input from the faculty and students. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Patrick Roberson, Chief Dental Officer/Associate Dean, Workman School of Dental Medicine at proberso@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Attending-Dentist--Open-Rank-Faculty-Clinician--Prosthodontics---Digital-Dentistry---Non-tenure-track_R0008899": {
      "title": "Attending Dentist, Open Rank Faculty Clinician (Prosthodontics & Digital Dentistry), Non-tenure track",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHPU Health- Oral Health Network is a non-for-profit dental network that provides primary and surgical/specialty care, part of the High Point University Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM). We are seeking full-time (12-month, non-tenure track) faculty appointments with duties in the High Point University Oral Health Network (OHN) and Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which includes the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. The faculty member in Prosthodontics and Digital Dentistry is responsible in providing patient care in OHN and educating pre-doctoral dental students and post-doctoral residents in WSDM. The position will report to the Chief Dental Officer and executive leadership team (ELT) of the Workman School of Dental Medicine. The position will report to the Chief Dental Officer. QUALIFICATIONS: Education DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent), active full dental licensure in the state of North Carolina Completion of a CODA-accredited prosthodontics program in the US. Must be at least board-eligible from the American Board of Prosthodontics Experience and Training Preferably 5 years of experience in clinical practice of dentistry Proficiency in digital applications in dentistry, including scanning, CAD-CAM 3-d printing, and digital treatment planning. Leadership experience and program building is preferrable. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Robust verbal and written communication skills Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU WSDM’s core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Clinical documentation, diagnosis, and treatment planning using electronic health records (EHR) such as EPIC systems. Travel to OHN (oral health network) sites Adaptability Coachability Integrity and innovation Trustworthy ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   The candidate selected for this position will perform all duties directed by the Chief Clinical Officer and WSDM executive leadership team (ELT). The candidate will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to: Patient care Provides comprehensive and emergency care to patients seen in the HPU Oral Health Network OHN) Demonstrates the highest level of professionalism, ethical-fitness, and patient-centered approach Documentation of patient history, examination findings, diagnosis, treatment planning utilizing electronic health record (EPIC) Comforts with digital technologies such as intraoral scanning, photography, 3d printing, CAD-CAM, and imaging. Provides restorative dentistry with emphasis on implantology. Be able to cover for other OHN providers, as needed. Education Serves as an attending clinical faculty for DMD and AEGD residents. May be involved in curriculum design and pre-clinical simulation lab courses. To develop a digital innovation lab for education and application for the HPU OHN. Provides continuing education courses in HPU WSDM as a content matter expert. Serves as a clinician role model for learners and be able to thrive in a start-up education model. ACCOUNTABILITY: Chief Dental Officer, Dean Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews is conducted along with an annual assessment by the CDO and includes input from the faculty and students. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Patrick Roberson, Clinical Associate Professor, General Dentistry and Public Health and Chief Dental Officer at proberso@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Attending-Dentist--Open-Rank-Faculty-Clinician--Endodontics---Non-tenure-track_R0008898": {
      "title": "Attending Dentist, Open Rank Faculty Clinician (Endodontics), Non-tenure track",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHPU Health- Oral Health Network is a non-for-profit dental network that provides primary and surgical/specialty care, part of the High Point University Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM). We are seeking full-time (12-month, non-tenure track) faculty appointments with duties in the High Point University Oral Health Network (OHN) and Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which includes the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. The faculty member in Endodontology is responsible in providing patient care in OHN and educating pre-doctoral dental students and post-doctoral residents in WSDM. The position will report to the Chief Dental Officer and executive leadership team (ELT) of the Workman School of Dental Medicine. The position will report to the Chief Dental Officer. QUALIFICATIONS: Education DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent), eligibility for dental licensure (instructor) in the state of North Carolina Completion of a CODA-accredited or equivalent foreign program in endodontics Experience and Training Preferably board-eligible from the American Board of Endodontics 5 years of experience in clinical practice of dentistry is preferred, but not required. Experience in dental education is preferred, but not required. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Robust verbal and written communication skills Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU WSDM’s core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Clinical documentation, diagnosis, and treatment planning using electronic health records (EHR) such as EPIC systems. Travel to OHN (oral health network) sites located within 1 hour of High Point, NC Commitment to and exemplary embodiment of core values of compassion, innovation, growth mindset, learning and leadership, integrity and trust. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   The candidate selected for this position will perform all duties directed by the Chief Dental Officer and WSDM executive leadership team (ELT). The candidate will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to: Patient care Provide comprehensive and emergency endodontic diagnosis and treatment patients seen in the HPU Oral Health Network OHN) Demonstrate the highest level of professionalism, ethical-fitness, and patient-centered approach Application of evidence-based practices to optimize patient outcomes Documentation of patient history, examination findings, diagnosis, treatment planning utilizing electronic health record (EPIC) Comfort with digital technologies such as surgical microscope, intraoral scanning, photography, 3d printing, CAD-CAM, and CBCT imaging. Be able to cover for other OHN providers, as needed. Education Serve as an attending clinical faculty for DMD and/or post-doctoral residents including modeling of optimal patient care, coaching in instructional and experiential environments, and assessment of learner performance Support curriculum content design and delivery in classroom-based and simulation-based learning environments. Provide continuing education courses in HPU WSDM as a content matter expert. Serve as a clinician role model for learners and be able to thrive in a start-up education model. ACCOUNTABILITY: Chief Dental Officer, with input from the Executive Leadership Team Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews is conducted along with an annual assessment by the CDO and includes input from the faculty and students. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Patrick Roberson, Clinical Associate Professor, General Dentistry and Public Health and Chief Dental Officer at proberso@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Attending-Dentist--Open-Rank-Faculty-Clinician--Orthodontics---Non-tenure-track_R0008823-2": {
      "title": "Attending Dentist, Open Rank Faculty Clinician (Orthodontics), Non-tenure track",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHPU Health- Oral Health Network is a non-for-profit dental network that provides primary and surgical/specialty care, part of the High Point University Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM). We are seeking part-time and full-time (12-month, non-tenure track) faculty appointments with duties in the High Point University Oral Health Network (OHN) and Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which includes the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs. The faculty member in Orthodontics is responsible for providing patient care in OHN and educating pre-doctoral dental students and post-doctoral residents in WSDM. The position will report to the Chief Dental Officer. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. QUALIFICATIONS: Education DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent), eligibility for dental licensure in the state of North Carolina Completion of a CODA-accredited or equivalent foreign program in orthodontics Experience and Training Preferably board-eligible from the American Board of Endodontics 5 years of experience in clinical practice of dentistry is preferred, but not required. Experience in dental education is preferred, but not required. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Robust verbal and written communication skills Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU WSDM’s core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Clinical documentation, diagnosis, and treatment planning using electronic health records (EHR) such as EPIC systems. Travel to OHN (oral health network) sites located within 1 hour of High Point, NC Commitment to and exemplary embodiment of core values of compassion, innovation, growth mindset, learning and leadership, integrity and trust. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   The candidate selected for this position will perform all duties directed by the Chief Dental  Officer. The candidate will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to: Patient care Provide comprehensive and emergency orthodontics and craniofacial orthopedic diagnosis and treatment patients seen in the HPU Oral Health Network OHN) Demonstrate the highest level of professionalism, ethical-fitness, and patient-centered approach Application of evidence-based practices to optimize patient outcomes Documentation of patient history, examination findings, diagnosis, treatment planning utilizing electronic health record (EPIC) Comfort with digital technologies such as intraoral scanning, photography, 3d printing, CAD-CAM, and CBCT imaging. Be able to cover for other OHN providers, as needed. Education Serve as an attending clinical faculty for DMD and/or post-doctoral residents including modeling of optimal patient care, coaching in instructional and experiential environments, and assessment of learner performance Support curriculum content design and delivery in classroom-based and simulation-based learning environments. Provide continuing education courses in HPU WSDM as a content matter expert. Serve as a clinician role model for learners and be able to thrive in a start-up education model. ACCOUNTABILITY: Chief Dental Officer, with input from the Executive Leadership Team Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews is conducted along with an annual assessment by the CDO and includes input from the faculty and students. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Ali Muhammad Shazib, Dean, Workman School of Dental Medicine at mshazib@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Program-Director--Dental-Anesthesiology_R0008860": {
      "title": "Program Director, Dental Anesthesiology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHigh Point University Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM) is seeking a full-time Program Director, Dental Anesthesiology. The Dental Anesthesiology Program Director serves as the academic, clinical, and administrative leader of the CODA-accredited Dental Anesthesiology Residency Program. The Program Director is responsible for the development, implementation, continuous evaluation, and improvement of all aspects of the residency program while maintaining compliance with Commission on Dental Accreditation (CODA) standards. This position provides leadership in curriculum development, resident recruitment and assessment, faculty development, outcomes assessment, quality assurance, patient safety, and program administration. The Program Director works collaboratively with WSDM leadership, HPU Health clinical sites, specialty faculty, and affiliated healthcare professionals to ensure residents receive comprehensive educational experiences that prepare them for independent practice in dental anesthesiology. The Program Director maintains an active clinical practice within the HPU Oral Health Network, providing anesthesia services, resident supervision, and direct patient care while serving as a role model for clinical excellence and professionalism. The position allocation consists of approximately: 60% Clinical Activities (3 days/week) 40% Administrative, Educational, and Scholarly Activities (2 days/week) Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Candidates must successfully complete a background check and credentialing process satisfactory to High Point University. QUALIFICATIONS:     R equ ired Qualifications   DDS or DMD degree from a   CODA accredited   institution   or   equ ivalent    Completion of a CODA-accredited Dental Anesthesiology Residency Program.    Board Eligible or Board Certified by the American Dental Board of Anesthesiology (ADBA).    Eligible for unrestricted dental licensure in North Carolina.    Current certification in BLS, ACLS, and PALS.    Demonstrated experience in administration of office-based anesthesia and hospital-based anesthesia services.    Demonstrated commitment to resident education and mentoring.    Preferred Qualifications   Previous   experience as a residency program director, associate program director, or educational leader.    Experience with CODA accreditation processes, self-studies, and site visits.    Experience in outcomes assessment, curriculum development, and faculty development.    Experience with quality improvement and patient safety initiatives.    Experience with simulation-based education.    Academic rank   commensurate   with qualifications and experience.    Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities   Comprehensive knowledge of dental   anesthesiology,   education,   and practice.    Understanding   CODA accreditation standards and residency program administration.    Strong leadership, communication, and organizational skills .     Ability to collaborate across disciplines and healthcare environments.    Experience with assessment systems, program evaluation, and educational outcomes.    Commitment to innovation, integrity, leadership, and teamwork.    Ability to thrive within a developing and evolving educational environment.     ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   Program Leadership and Administration   Provide overall leadership and management of the Dental Anesthesiology Residency Program.    Develop and   maintain   program goals,   objectives , competencies, and assessment processes.    Ensure ongoing compliance with CODA accreditation standards.    Lead program self-study, annual reporting, accreditation documentation, and site visit preparation.    Manage program   budgets   in collaboration with WSDM leadership.    Participate in strategic planning and program development initiatives.    Maintain resident policies, manuals, and program documentation.      Curriculum Development and Educational Oversight   Develop, implement, and continuously evaluate the didactic and clinical curriculum.    Ensure residents achieve competency in all r equ ired areas of dental anesthesiology.     Coordinate educational experiences across clinical and hospital environments.    Integrate evidence-based practice, patient safety, quality improvement, and interprofessional education into the curriculum.    Monitor educational outcomes and implement program improvements as   indicated   by assessment data.    Facilitate resident seminars, case conferences, morbidity and mortality reviews, journal clubs, and simulation exercises.      Resident Recruitment, Evaluation, and Mentorship   Direct resident recruitment, application review, interviewing,   selection , and onboarding processes.    Provide ongoing mentoring and professional development for residents.    Conduct resident evaluations and competency assessments.    Develop in div idualized learning plans and remediation strategies when necessary.    Ensure residents receive   timely   feedback   regarding   academic and clinical performance.    Monitor resident well-being and professional development.      Faculty Development and Collaboration   Recruit, orient, and support participating faculty.    Promote faculty calibration and consistency in resident assessment.    Facilitate faculty development activities related to teaching, evaluation, and clinical supervision.    Collaborate with specialty and interdisciplinary faculty to enhance educational experiences.      Quality Assurance, Patient Safety, and Outcomes Assessment   Oversee quality assurance and quality improvement activities related to anesthesia services.    Monitor patient safety outcomes and resident clinical performance.    Review adverse events, complications, and   inc ident reports.    Develop and   maintain   program outcomes assessment systems.    Analyze resident achievement, procedural experience, and program effectiveness data.    Implement continuous quality improvement initiatives.      Clinical Responsibilities (3 Days Per Week)   Provide direct   anesthesia   for   patient care within the HPU Oral Health Network.    Supervise residents during anesthesia care and patient management.    Participate in preoperative assessment, anesthesia delivery, recovery management, and emergency preparedness activities.    Ensure compliance with institutional policies, state regulations, and professional standards.    Serve as a clinical mentor and role model for residents and faculty.    Participate in interdisciplinary treatment planning and patient care conferences.      Scholarly Activity   Support resident scholarly activity, research, and quality improvement projects.    Participate in professional organizations related to dental anesthesiology and health professions education.    Contribute to scholarly dissemination, presentations, and publications.    Promote evidence-based practice throughout the residency program.     ACCOUNTABILITY:     Report   directly to the A ssociate Dean of Postgraduate Dental Education .    Collaborates closely with the Dean, Chief Dental Officer, Graduate Medical Education partners, and specialty faculty.    Receives annual performance evaluation from WSDM leadership with input from residents, faculty, and clinical personnel.    Responsible for   maintaining   program compliance with CODA accreditation standards and institutional r equ irements.   For more information regarding this position please contact Dr. Muhammad Ali Shazib, Dean, Workman School of Dental Medicine  at mshazib@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor--Actuarial-Science-and-Statistics_R0007998": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor, Actuarial Science and Statistics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Department of Mathematical Sciences at High Point University invites applications for a full-time Assistant or Associate Professor of Actuarial Science and Statistics, with an expected start date of August 2027. This position is a 9-month, non-tenure track position, eligible for renewable multi-year contracts and eventual promotion to Associate Professor or Professor rank. We seek a creative and thoughtful teacher-scholar to join our dynamic team and take the lead in teaching and mentoring our students pursuing the B.S. in Actuarial Science for the long term. The department also offers undergraduate programs in Mathematics, Mathematical Economics, and Data Analytics and Statistics. The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate mathematics and/or statistics courses within the Mathematical Sciences, teaching not only our majors but also serving other STEM undergraduates and general education students. For this position, we seek a person whose academic and/or professional expertise equips them to teach upper-division mathematics and statistics courses to Actuarial Science students. Additional expectations include academic advising, department service (e.g. assessment, recruitment), serving on school and university-wide committees. Faculty are expected to develop and maintain an active program of professional development, and involving undergraduates in those endeavors is a plus. The typical teaching load is 12 credit hours per semester, which equates to three 4-credit courses each term. QUALIFICATIONS: Education Candidates must have an earned PhD or doctorate in Statistics, Applied Mathematics, Mathematics, or a closely related field. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: The successful candidate should have demonstrated promise of excellence in teaching, a record of scholarly achievement, a collaborative mindset, and an interest in working with highly motivated undergraduate students. Additionally, the successful candidate will present evidence of the potential to establish industry partnerships for internship opportunities for students in Actuarial Science. The success of our undergraduate students is our primary focus. Responsibilities: Teach 24 contact hours (typically 6 classes) per year Undertake professional development and produce scholarly research Advise students Assist with curriculum development and department assessment Assist with university and department recruiting efforts Participate in department, school, and university meetings and committees Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair and/or Dean Founded in 1924, HPU is a 102-year-old liberal arts institution located in the Piedmont Triad region of North Carolina. At High Point University, every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people. “America’s Best Colleges” 2025 Edition, published in the U.S. News & World Report, ranks HPU #1 among all regional colleges in the South and #1 as Most Innovative Regional College in the South for innovative improvements in terms of curriculum, faculty, students, campus life, technology or facilities. All applicants must submit a single attachment with the following sections: A letter of interest addressing the required qualifications and responsibilities A current CV A statement of teaching philosophy A statement of research interests Unofficial transcripts of graduate studies Names and contact information for three professional recommendations Any questions related to this position should be sent to Dr. Jenny Sharpe, Chair of Mathematical Science, jsharpe1@highpoint.edu . Applications received by October 2, 2026 are assured full consideration.  The start date for the position is August 2027. Applicants who do not meet the qualifications or are not legally authorized to work in the US will not be considered."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Art-and-Graphic-Design_R0006569": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Art and Graphic Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Department of Art and Graphic Design is housed in the David R. Hayworth School of Arts and Design at High Point University. The department is expanding and requires the addition of a new adjunct instructor to help us deliver foundation courses within our Studio Art and Graphic Design degrees. Our programs are growing and we are seeking adjunct faculty to help us deliver potential courses in Art Appreciation, Fundamentals of Design, Drawing, and Digital Design. High Point University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Terminal degree (MFA or equivalent) in Studio Art, Graphic Design or a closely related field. Some experience teaching at the college/university level Be a good communicator, collaborator and team player who can thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced, environment RESPONSIBILITIES: Potentially teach undergraduate courses in Art Appreciation, Fundamentals of Design, Drawing, and Digital Art and Design. For any questions related to the position, please contact Mark Brown, Chair and Associate Professor at mabrown@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Computer-Engineering_R0008850": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Webb School of Engineering at High Point University is seeking part-time Adjunct Instructors in Electrical and Computer Engineering. We are looking to fill sections of Electrical and Computer Engineering courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. Teaching responsibilities will include lectures and labs in a variety of areas of the discipline, with particular interest in power and controls. Other duties include promptly communicating with students, meeting with students as necessary to facilitate learning, and collecting assessment data necessary for the ABET accreditation process. Qualifications Education A minimum of a master’s degree in electrical or computer engineering, or a closely related field is required; a Ph.D. and college-level teaching experience are preferred. Relevant industrial experience is also regarded as desirable. Applications should include the following items, submitted as a single document: (i) a cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position, (ii) curriculum vitae, (iii) an unofficial transcript with the highest awarded degree, and (iv) names and contact information for three professional references. At least one reference should be able to address the applicant’s potential or experience in teaching. For additional information, please contact Dr. Michael Oudshoorn, Chair and Professor, Electrical and Computer Engineering, at moudshoo@highpoint.edu. Apply online at https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Highpoint-Faculty High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas for part time positions. High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information or veteran status and other legally protected statuses.  The University encourages all applicants to apply."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Electrical-and-Computer-Engineering_R0008849": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Webb School of Engineering at High Point University invites applications for a full-time faculty position at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor of Computer Engineering, with an expected start date of January 1, 2027. A later start date is feasible. The successful candidate will join the Department of Computer Science and Electrical Engineering and contribute to the continued growth of computing and engineering programs within the School. We seek a creative, dynamic, and student-centered teacher-scholar who will play an important role in delivering high-quality undergraduate instruction, developing innovative and active-learning classroom and laboratory experiences, mentoring students, pursuing scholarly research, and contributing to department, school, university, and professional service. The successful candidate will teach a variety of undergraduate courses in Computer Engineering and related areas. While research specialization is open, the successful candidate is likely to teach courses such as Real-Time and Embedded Systems; Computer Architecture; Digital Logic and Computer Systems; Microprocessor Applications; Digital Signal Processing; and related courses in computer engineering, electrical engineering, and computing systems. Additional expectations include academic advising, supporting undergraduate research, assisting with curriculum development and assessment, contributing to ABET accreditation efforts, supporting student recruitment and retention, and serving on department, school, and university committees. Faculty appointments are for a nine-month contract period with a normal teaching load of 12 contact hours per semester. Qualifications Education Candidates must have an earned Ph.D. or doctorate in Computer Engineering or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Knowledge, Skills, and Ability The successful candidate should have demonstrated promise of excellence in undergraduate teaching, evidence of scholarly achievement or strong potential for scholarly productivity, and an interest in working with highly motivated undergraduate students. Candidates should be committed to student success, experiential learning, undergraduate research, and the development of innovative laboratory and project-based educational experiences. The preferred candidate will demonstrate one or more of the following: Ability to teach core and advanced undergraduate courses in Computer Engineering; Experience with laboratory-based instruction in areas such as embedded systems, digital logic, computer architecture, microprocessor applications, digital signal processing, or related areas; Interest in mentoring undergraduate research projects, design projects, or competition teams; Potential to develop partnerships with industry, government agencies, or other academic institutions; Interest in contributing to curriculum development, assessment, and ABET accreditation activities; A collaborative mindset and a desire to contribute to a growing engineering and computing environment. Responsibilities The successful candidate will be expected to: Teach 12 contact hours per semester ; Teach undergraduate courses in Computer Engineering and related areas; Advise and mentor students; Pursue scholarly research or creative activity, especially in partnership with undergraduate students; Assist with curriculum development, assessment, and ABET accreditation; Support student recruitment, retention, and success initiatives; Participate in department, school, and university meetings and committees; Engage in service activities at the department, school, university, and professional levels; Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair and/or Dean. About High Point University Founded in 1924, High Point University is a 101-year-old liberal arts institution located in the Piedmont Triad region of North Carolina. At High Point University, every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people. “America’s Best Colleges” 2025 Edition, published in U.S. News & World Report , ranks HPU #1 among all regional colleges in the South and #1 as Most Innovative Regional College in the South for innovative improvements in curriculum, faculty, students, campus life, technology, and facilities. The Webb School of Engineering offers innovative programs designed to produce well-rounded graduates with strong technical skills and the necessary life skills to be successful engineers and computer scientists. The Department of Computer Science and Electrical Engineering supports undergraduate programs in computing, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence and data science, electrical engineering, and computer engineering. Application Process All applicants must submit a single attachment with the following sections: A letter of interest addressing the required qualifications and responsibilities; A current curriculum vitae; A statement of teaching philosophy; A statement of research interests; Unofficial transcripts of graduate and undergraduate education; Names and contact information for three professional references. Applications must be submitted through the university’s job site: https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/Highpoint-Faculty Applications received by September 1, 2026 are assured full consideration. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. The start date for the position is January 1, 2027 . Applicants who do not meet the qualifications or are not legally authorized to work in the United States will not be considered. Any questions related to this position should be sent to Dr. Michael Oudshoorn, Dean of Engineering , at moudshoo@highpoint.edu . Choose to be Extraordinary!"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank-Faculty-Position-in-Multimedia-Journalism-and-Sports-Media_R0008846": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position in Multimedia Journalism and Sports Media",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Nido R. Qubein School of Communication at High Point University invites applications for a full time, open rank faculty position in Multimedia Journalism and Sports Media. We seek a dynamic educator and engaged professional who can contribute to two highly experiential programs grounded in innovation, storytelling, and real world media practice. Candidates with strengths in either multimedia journalism, sports media, or the intersection of both areas are encouraged to apply. This position is designed to support instruction across multimedia journalism and sports media, with flexibility in rank based on qualifications and experience. Rank will be commensurate with academic preparation, teaching record, professional achievement, and potential for scholarship. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty committed to excellence in teaching, mentorship, and industry connected learning. This is a nine month renewable contract appointment with a standard 3/3 teaching load or ¾ teaching load, based on rank. Qualifications Required Qualifications Master’s degree in journalism, sports media, communication, mass communication, or a closely related field. Evidence of successful college level teaching experience and/or significant relevant professional industry experience. Ability to teach in areas related to multimedia journalism and sports media. Commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and student mentorship. Strong communication and collaborative skills. Preferred Qualifications Preference may be given to candidates with experience in one or more of the following: Multimedia reporting and storytelling Sports media production and content creation Broadcast, digital, or multimedia journalism Data journalism Student media advising or experiential learning supervision Industry partnerships or professional media engagement Record of scholarship, creative activity, or professional accomplishment appropriate to rank Responsibilities Primary responsibilities include: Teaching Teach undergraduate courses in multimedia journalism and sports media, based on expertise and departmental needs. Contribute to a hands on, professionally oriented curriculum that emphasizes storytelling, reporting, content creation, audience engagement, and emerging media practices. Incorporate contemporary tools, technologies, and professional workflows into instruction. Support experiential learning through student media, live productions, field coverage, or related applied opportunities when appropriate. Contribute to curriculum development and ongoing program innovation. Advising and Mentorship Advise and mentor undergraduate students in academic planning, career preparation, and professional development. Support student success through engaged faculty mentorship and participation in a student-centered academic environment. Service Participate in school, departmental, and university committee work. Contribute to faculty governance, assessment, recruitment efforts, and other service activities that support the mission of the School and University. Collaborate with colleagues on initiatives that advance program growth and industry engagement. Scholarship and Professional Engagement Depending on rank and appointment, engage in scholarly, creative, and/or professional activity appropriate to the position. Maintain professional currency in journalism, sports media, or related communication fields. Application Materials Applicants should submit: Cover letter addressing qualifications, teaching interests, and fit for the position Curriculum vitae Unofficial transcript for highest degree earned Contact information for three professional references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For more information, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Professor Ken Medlin, at kmedlin1@highpoint.edu"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Dean--Webb-School-of-Engineering_R0008832": {
      "title": "Dean, Webb School of Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis is a full-time, 12-month, faculty position. The Dean of the Webb School of Engineering provides strategic leadership for the academic programs, faculty, and operations of the School, including Engineering, Computer Science, and Mathematical Sciences, and ensures alignment with the mission and priorities of the University. The Dean leads the development and execution of a forward-looking vision for the School, including curriculum innovation, enrollment growth, and program differentiation. The Dean is responsible for maintaining and securing appropriate accreditations (including ABET), recruiting and developing exceptional, student-focused faculty and staff, and expanding high-impact experiential learning opportunities. The Dean collaborates with admissions and university leadership to advance program visibility, student recruitment, and institutional reputation and provides leadership for all departments and academic programs within the School. QUALIFICATIONS: Education A doctorate in an engineering discipline from an accredited School of Engineering is preferred. Applicants holding doctorates in related fields will be considered. Experience and Training Minimum of three to five years of academic program administration and leadership experience Demonstrated track record of teaching excellence and scholarly productivity commensurate with a lead academic officer of a School Proven track record of meeting the requirements of ABET accreditation Exceptional organizational, interpersonal, collaborative, team building, and communication skills (written and oral) Experience in managing complex budgets Demonstrated effectiveness in developing strategic industry partnerships Demonstrated ability to unite faculty across multiple disciplines or departments in pursuit of shared academic and strategic goals. Knowledge, Skills, Ability Demonstrated understanding of technology use and AI applications in education and their potential impact on teaching and learning Strong leadership and management skills Demonstrated ability to explain complex technical concepts to non-technical audiences Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Excellent communication and interpersonal abilities Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in the representation of High Point University Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Shared commitment to High Point University’s core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Adaptability Innovation Integrity Trustworthiness ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :  The candidate selected for this position will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to: Curriculum Takes the lead with ABET accreditation of programs Provides curricular leadership by initiating, sustaining, delivering, and/or modifying the curriculum in accordance with ABET accreditation standards as well as school and university-wide strategic planning goals Fosters the development and delivery of “best practices” in teaching both within the classroom and through strategic industry partnerships Regularly reviews and evaluates the curriculum for appropriate rigor and breadth Identifies industry partners that provide exceptional experiences for senior design projects, internships, co-ops, and other high impact practices for students Faculty & Staff Develops and executes long-range staffing plans (for faculty and support staff) that are aligned with curriculum delivery and enrollment Ensures that faculty and staff are informed of ABET accreditation standards and organizational and educational policies that affect the delivery of educational services and operations of the program Mentors and oversees faculty growth, scholarship, and professional development Ensures documented curriculum and course assessment through development of learning objectives, identification of appropriate teaching strategies, and collection of data and feedback to ensure academic excellence, integrity of the program, and alignment with ABET standards Prepares annual performance reviews for all faculty and staff Directs and coordinates activities of academic advisors and departmental staff to ensure timely delivery of quality services Learners Mediates between students and faculty in appropriate and legal ways; facilitates the resolution of disagreement or conflict between faculty and students Advises students on professional options within their chosen field Prepares letters of reference for learners Develops and expands appropriate alumni and community relationships General Academic and Operational Responsibilities Provides the necessary leadership to advance the education mission of the university and the school and promotes a climate that is responsive, focused and innovative Keeps current on trends in higher education and pursues opportunities for improvement within their field Actively participates in marketing of the programs and represents the school and university to prospective students, professional organizations, potential future employers for students, and any other relevant constituencies Provides strategic oversight of school facilities, ensuring safe, efficient, and innovative learning and research environments Maintains and enhances the already excellent reputation of the school and university Advises the Provost, Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs, and the President on academic matters Performs other assignments on an ad hoc basis, as required Is fiscally responsible For more information regarding this position, please contact Rhonda Grimsley, Executive Assistant, Office of the Provost at rgrimsley@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Visiting-Assistant-Professor--Criminal-Justice_R0008821": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Department of Criminal Justice at High Point University invites applications for a faculty position for the 2026-2027 academic year, at the rank of visiting assistant professor (preferred), with part-time being possible. A search for a full-time position will be launched during the academic year, and visiting faculty, with interest, are invited to apply. The position begins in August of 2026 and candidates with a master’s degree in criminal justice, a J.D., or a closely related field and applicable field experience will be strongly considered. A PhD in criminal justice and J.D. or a closely related field is preferred. Scheduled courses for fall 2026 mainly revolve around criminal law and mock trial. Ability to teach various law related courses is required. Ability to teach violent crime, intro to criminal justice, and help with international security courses is desired but not required. Duties include teaching three or four courses per semester (depending on rank and credentials) and performing departmental service, as part of a close and vital faculty team. The University seeks applicants who are committed to education as an experiential and life-enhancing process. To apply, submit as one electronic document: 1) a cover letter; 2) curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy, methods and examples of classroom practice; 4) a copy of all graduate transcripts with degree(s) awarded; and 5) names and contact information for three professional references. Submit questions to Dr. Alec Szalewski. aszalews@highpoint.edu QUALIFICATIONS: Education Master’s in criminal justice or closely related field and experience J.D. in criminal justice or closely related field and experience Ph. D. in criminal justice or closely related field preferred; ABD welcome Experience and Training Prefer prior teaching experience, especially in the following courses: criminal law, courts and trials, crime, law & national security, mock trial, criminal evidence, and international criminal justice Ability to teach violent crime or into to the justice system is beneficial but not required Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Knowledge of the above course subjects ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   Teach three or four courses per semester depending on qualifications and rank and perform departmental service.    ACCOUNTABILITY: Report to Chair of the Department of Criminal Justice, the Dean of the School of the Douglas S. Witcher School of Humanities and Behavioral Sciences, and to the Provost of the University."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Marketing_R0004131": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business at High Point University is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Marketing. We are looking to fill sections of Marketing courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Cynthia Hanson, Chair of the Department of Marketing at chanson@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: Ph.D. in the teaching discipline preferred; a master’s degree and/or appropriate professional experience in the teaching discipline will be considered. Upload an unofficial copy of your Ph.D. and/or a master’s transcript.  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  This will be used to verify you have at least 18 graduate semester hours in Marketing. Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). If you have less than 18 hours, we will consider your commensurate experience/training.  Be sure this is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches Marketing at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor_R0008754": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Kenneth F. Kahn School of Law at High point University Schol of Law is seeking applications from experienced lawyers, judges, and legal professionals to join our pool of adjunct faculty. Adjunct Instructor teach specialized, upper-level doctrinal courses or experiential, skills-based courses. We are looking for practitioners with deep subject matter expertise who are committed to preparing the next generation of attorneys by providing practical, real-world insights. The selected candidate will work in a highly collaborative environment that fosters critical analysis, reasoned argument, and the free exchange of ideas and equips students with the doctrinal knowledge, practical skills, and professional values needed for success in a rapidly evolving legal profession. Candidates should possess an entrepreneurial spirit and be well-suited to work in a collegial and student-oriented culture. Required Qualifications Education:  Juris Doctor (J.D.) from an ABA-accredited law school. Experience:  A minimum of [3-5] years of active, high-level practice experience in the relevant field of law. Licensure:  Active, good-standing membership in at least one State Bar. Skills:  Strong communication, interpersonal, and presentation skills. Commitment:  Demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, and student mentorship. Preferred Qualifications Prior teaching experience at a law school or graduate level. Record of scholarly publications or presentations in the specialized field. Experience in clinical legal education or skill-based instruction. Expected Competencies Subject Matter Expertise:  Deep knowledge in the specific area relating to the course(s) you are interested in teaching Professionalism:  Ability to represent the Law School with integrity Flexibility:  Ability to adapt teaching methods to diverse learning styles. Position Description & Responsibilities: Course Development & Delivery:  Develop and deliver a rigorous, engaging course syllabus that meets academic standards and complies with the school’s learning outcomes. Teaching:  Conduct in-person or online classes, facilitating discussions, lectures, and interactive simulations. Assessment & Grading:  Create and grade exams, papers, or practical simulations (e.g., mock trials, contract drafting exercises). Provide timely and constructive feedback to students regarding their performance. Student Support:  Maintain regular \"office hours\" (in-person or virtual) to advise students on course materials and career paths. Technology Utilization:  Utilize the institution's Learning Management System (Blackboard) for posting syllabi, assignments, and grades. Collaboration & Compliance:  Collaborate with full-time faculty to ensure curriculum alignment; attend mandatory adjunct orientation/meetings; adhere to all university, ABA, and FERPA policies. To apply, please submit the following materials in a single document: 1. Curriculum Vitae (CV). 2. A letter of Interest detailing the course(s) you are interested in teaching and any prior teaching experience. 3. List of three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, so interested individuals are encouraged to apply as soon as possible. For more information regarding this position, please contact Katharine Van Tassel , Professor of Law and chair of the law school’s hiring committee, at kvantass@highpoint.edu. The Kahn School of Law is one of the most recent graduate schools begun by High Point University, an innovative liberal arts institution with 6,000 undergraduate and graduate students. The School of Law is currently seeking ABA provisional approval in conformity with ABA Standards."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank-Entrepreneurship-Faculty---Department-Chair_R0008712": {
      "title": "Open Rank Entrepreneurship Faculty & Department Chair",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe David S. Congdon School of Entrepreneurship (CSE) at High Point University is seeking a new colleague to lead the Entrepreneurship program as Chair and Faculty member. The successful candidate will join High Point University’s CSE leadership team, have substantial industry/entrepreneurial experience (at least 10 years) through entrepreneurial venture development, teaching, practice, or business ownership experience. They will also bring the leadership skills necessary to manage departmental operations and support academic excellence. A master’s degree in Entrepreneurship, Business, or other relevant major is required, and a PhD in Entrepreneurship or Business is preferred. At HPU, teaching and student engagement are paramount. The Chair is expected to teach at a reduced load with an emphasis on application, industry engagement, and experiential learning. Based on research and/or specialty areas, there may be opportunities for curricular development in those specialties. As the Entrepreneurship Department Chair, the candidate is also responsible for: strategic planning and initiatives development; faculty leadership and oversight (staffing, scheduling, supervision, mentoring, etc.); development and oversight of some entrepreneurial events; and student engagement. Essential Qualifications: A PhD in Entrepreneurship or Business (preferred). A commitment to quality teaching, professional growth, and university service. Be a strong communicator, collaborator, and team player who can thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced, extraordinary environment. At least 10 years of professional entrepreneurial experience or equivalent experience in business start-ups. Organized with the ability to work independently and operate efficiently within a team environment. Preference will be given to candidates with university-level teaching and experience in academic administration or leadership roles. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Represent and advance the mission and values of High Point University and the David S. Congdon School of Entrepreneurship. Collaborate with the Dean, CSE Leadership Team, and campus partners on strategic initiatives, curriculum design, and delivery. Teaching: Teach entrepreneurship and related disciplines as assigned; develop and deliver curriculum aligned with current entrepreneurial business practices and experiential learning. Advise and mentor students on academic progress, venture development, and career pathways. Maintain active engagement with the entrepreneurial community to strengthen instructional relevance and expand student opportunities. Student Engagement/Recruitment: Manage and support student entrepreneurship programming, including internal and external competitions, showcases, and alumni engagement, as well as administration of internal donor-related grant funding. Participate in university recruitment, promotional efforts, and retention activities to support enrollment and engagement of prospective and current students. Department Chair Responsibilities Provide administrative leadership for the Entrepreneurship Department, including strategic planning, program development, and operational oversight. Manage course scheduling, faculty workload assignments, staffing needs, resource allocation, and fiscal planning. Conduct faculty evaluations and support professional development. Support accreditation and continuous improvement by participating in annual assessment activities, including the coordination of required documentation and reporting. Collect, analyze, and report program data for performance metrics and donor-grant reporting to ensure effectiveness and accountability. Serve as the primary liaison between the department, the David S. Congdon School of Entrepreneurship, and other university units; facilitate effective communication among faculty, staff, students, and administration. Service and Engagement Represent and advocate for the program, school, and university at internal and external events, including recruitment activities. Maintain active professional development. Serve on department, school, university, and relevant community/professional/governmental committees. Support institutional initiatives related to student success, academic quality, and community engagement. Develop and maintain partnerships with industry, alumni, and community organizations to enhance program visibility and student opportunities. Working Conditions Work is performed in standard office and classroom environments. Occasional evening or weekend responsibilities may be required for events, recruitment, or departmental activities. Some travel may be required for professional development or external engagement. Application Requirements: Screening of applications will begin upon receipt. Priority will be given to applications meeting the screening criteria; however, the position will remain open until filled. Applicants should upload the following documents in one PDF file : Cover letter briefly addressing your qualifications, teaching philosophy, professional history, and interest in this leadership and teaching role in the department. Current CV with complete professional and academic history. Unofficial transcripts of all degrees. Name, email, and phone contact information for three (3) references Only complete packages electronically submitted in Workday will be considered and reviewed. For additional information regarding this position, please contact Dean Flanders-Stec at lflanders@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank--Non-Tenure-Track--Professional-Sales-Faculty_R0008713": {
      "title": "Open Rank, Non-Tenure Track, Professional Sales Faculty",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe David S. Congdon School of Entrepreneurship at High Point University is searching for a new colleague to teach in the Professional Sales program. The successful candidate will have at least 10 years of professional experience as well as clear evidence of leadership, reputation and advancement in the selling profession. A master’s or equivalent degree with some professional sales experience is required. The successful candidate could teach a variety of undergraduate sales courses, such as Selling, Negotiating, Sales Leadership, and Retail Selling. In addition, depending upon qualifications, there will be an opportunity to add more specialized courses. The regular teaching load at HPU is three or four, four-credit-hour courses per semester on a 9-month contract with the opportunity for summer teaching. In addition, the successful candidate will have other administrative responsibilities such as academic advising and university service. Essential Qualifications: A commitment to quality teaching, professional growth, and university service. Being a good communicator, collaborator and team player who can thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced, extraordinary environment. University-level teaching experience is preferred but not required. Education: A master’s or equivalent degree with some professional experience is required. Essential Functions: Provide mentorship and advice to students in and beyond the classroom. Maintain a professional self-development program. Act as a representative and advocate for the program, school, and university. Participate in committees within the department, school, and university, Undertake other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the department chair. Application Requirements: Screening of applications will begin upon receipt. Priority will be given to applicants who meet the screening deadline; however, the position will remain open until it is filled. Applicants should upload the following documents in one PDF file : A cover letter briefly addressing your qualifications, teaching philosophy, professional history, and interest teaching in the program. A current resume with complete professional and academic history. An unofficial transcript of your highest degree awarded. The name, email, and phone contact information for three (3) references. Only complete packages electronically submitted will be considered and reviewed. High Point University can interview only those who are qualified to work in the USA. For additional information regarding this position, please contact: Professor Larry Quinn at lquinn@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Accounting_R0004126": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Accounting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business at High Point University is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Accounting. We are looking to fill sections of Accounting courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Christina Griffith, Chair and Professor of the Practice, at cgriffit@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: Ph.D. in the teaching discipline preferred; a master’s degree and/or appropriate professional experience in the teaching discipline will be considered. Upload an unofficial copy of your Ph.D. and/or a master’s transcript.  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  This will be used to verify you have at least 18 graduate semester hours in Accounting. Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). If you have less than 18 hours, we will consider your commensurate experience/training.  Be sure this is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches Accounting at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Director-of-Service-Learning--Open-Rank-Faculty-Position--10-months_R0008707": {
      "title": "Director of Service Learning, Open Rank Faculty Position, 10 months",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHigh Point University is currently seeking a full time Director of Service Learning. The Director of Service Learning will oversee all aspects of the Service Learning Program. As appropriate the Director of Service Learning will coordinate activities with the Executive Director of the HPU Center for Community Engagement. The Service Learning Program includes only curricular-based Service Learning courses. The director must be a university faculty member, with expertise in teaching Service Learning courses. The director will be responsible for all faculty recruitment, training, continuing education, student learning assessment, community partner relationships, oversight of the Social Innovation Minor, and program development. The position comes with appropriate course releases, so the director will teach a minimum 1-1 course load. This is not a remote work position. QUALIFICATIONS: Education Required doctorate or other terminal degree Preferred 3–5 years of experience in service learning and community engagement work. Strong understanding of experiential education and civic engagement principles.  Excellent communication, leadership, and organizational skills.  Experience and Training HPU faculty member  Experience teaching Service Learning courses  Background in the best practices of sustainable service  Experience in working with community partners, service programs, and a wide range of campus populations  Experience developing interdisciplinary curricular programs focused on deep and integrated learning, critical reflection, and related and assessable learning outcomes  Ability to conduct assessments and help faculty improve their courses based on feedback from students, community leaders and best instructional practices  Experience building partnerships with a varied population of constituents, including but not limited to students, faculty, staff, community leaders, and leaders in the field  Research and publication background in Service Learning is preferred  Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Strong communication skills  Ability to mediate issues between faculty, students, and community partners  Strong management skills  Familiarity with best practices in civic engagement and service learning  Familiarity with, or/and the ability to become familiar with, the needs, assets, and key players in the City of High Point and surrounding areas ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   Recruit HPU faculty to become trained to teach Service Learning courses. About 5-10 faculty per year should be trained.  Train HPU faculty to teach Service Learning courses. Host regular workshops to help faculty learn best practices in Service Learning and develop quality syllabi, community partner relationships and impactful student experiences.  Manage the Service Learning courses taught each semester. Ensure faculty have quality community partnerships, problem-solve issues that arise in classes, etc.  Assess the learning in all Service Learning courses through assessments of every Service Learning course which are aligned with the Office of Research and Planning.  Use assessment data to improve course instruction.  Provide continuing education and mentoring to faculty as they teach their SL courses.  Represent SL at Presidential Scholars, Open Houses, and other events as needed. Engage community partners, help build the capacity of partner sites to handle Service Learning students, and create stronger connections between faculty and the community.  Oversee and build the Service Learning Scholars Program, tracking students through the program and awarding students when they successfully complete it.  Research, present, and publish in the field of Service Learning, highlighting HPU’s distinctive model of Service Learning and increasing the university’s visibility.  Recruit faculty to attend and present at Service Learning conferences.  Encourage faculty to publish in the field of Service Learning.  Ensure proper protection of minors policies are followed for all SL courses and activities.  Chair the Service Learning Faculty Committee  Work with the Director of General Education to ensure alignment of SL offerings with the needs and work of the General Education program  Update the Service Learning website as needed.  Coordinate Service Learning stories with the Office of Communications.  Perform other site and position specific functions as assigned.  ACCOUNTABILITY: This position reports to the Provost and the Executive Director of the HPU Center of Community Engagement.  The Provost is the primary supervisor of this position. For more information regarding this position please contact Dr. Daniel Erb, Provost, at derb@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Assistant-Associate-Professor--Social-Personality-Psychology-and-Industrial-Organizational-Psychology_R0008656": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Social/Personality Psychology and Industrial/Organizational Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHigh Point University, Department of Psychology, is seeking qualified candidates for two full-time faculty positions at the undergraduate level beginning August 2027. These are Non-Tenure Track Positions for Social/Personality Psychology and Industrial/Organizational Psychology. Non-Tenure Track positions are eligible for promotion, with standards for teaching, scholarship, and service reviewed both internally and externally, typically in the sixth year. Qualifications: Successful candidates will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and student mentorship.  Teaching responsibilities include Introduction to Psychology, Research Methods, and established departmental courses within the applicant’s area of training. Candidates should be actively engaged in scholarship. Doctorate in Psychology is required at the time of employment. High Point University is a medium-sized, liberal arts university in central North Carolina, with approximately 5,000 undergraduate students. The Psychology Department offers a B.S. in psychology with approximately 230 majors and 125 minors. Instructions: Submit an application, including: cover letter, vita, a statement of teaching philosophy and experience, as well as evidence of teaching excellence, a statement of research interests, reprints, or pre-prints, and three confidential letters of recommendation. Graduate transcripts will be required later in the process. All application materials must be submitted by September 15, 2026. Please submit your application packet for the Social/Personality Psychology and the Industrial/Organizational Psychology Assistant/Associate Professor position here. If you have questions regarding these positions, please contact Dr. Deborah Danzis, Associate Professor of Psychology, at ddanzis@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank-Visiting-Faculty-Position--History_R0008635": {
      "title": "Open Rank Visiting Faculty Position, History",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Department of History at High Point University is seeking a Visiting Historian serving one academic year between the first full week of August 3, 2026 and May 7, 2027. Needs for this position include ability to teach US history courses and topical/thematic courses appropriate to the applicant’s research expertise and/or teaching experience. Please note that the Department is also opening a search for two full-time positions for a fall 2027 start.  Passion for teaching within a university liberal arts core is essential. Teaching load for this visiting position is variable (3:3, 3:4, or 4:4) depending on applicant’s strengths and highest degree in hand at the start of employment. A record of exceptional teaching and, at minimum, an M.A. in History or relevant field (i.e. American studies, Public History) by August 2026 are required. Duties will include some service to the university, to the Douglas S. Witcher School of Humanities and Behavioral Science, and the History Department. This includes, but may not be limited to, participation in institutional activities; active engagement in student learning outside of the classroom; and upholding the university's values and advancing its mission in recruiting situations. Candidates must apply through the university website. Applicants should submit a CV, a cover letter that explains their scholarly expertise in the field, and a teaching philosophy.  Additional materials may be requested later, such as transcripts, writing samples, recommendation letters, and performance evaluations."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Assistant-Associate-Rank--Non-Tenure-Track-Faculty--Athletic-Training_R0008547-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Rank, Non-Tenure Track Faculty, Athletic Training",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking a team-oriented athletic training faculty member (Full-time, 9 months) to join a dynamic inter-professional core of clinician-scientists in the Department of Athletic Training in the Congdon School of Health Sciences. This faculty member will primarily teach courses dedicated to Orthopedic Assessment, Optimizing Athletic Performance, and Evidence-Based Practice in the CAATE accredited professional Master of Science in Athletic Training program. Faculty members in the Department of Athletic Training are afforded a differential workload allowing for customization of expectations based on research expertise, clinical/teaching expertise, and service obligations. SUBMIT IN ONE COMBINED FILE: a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and a list of 3 references. For questions, please contact the search committee chair, Jolene Henning, EdD, ATC at jhenning@highpoint.edu. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS : Earned academic or clinical doctorate in athletic training or related field. Current BOC certification. Eligible for an NC athletic training license ATTRIBUTES OF THE IDEAL CANDIDATE: The ideal candidate will have: a minimum of 5 years of full-time clinical experience. prior experience teaching in higher education. research interests that align with sports science/data analytics, lower extremity biomechanics, youth sports, or injury prevention. Evidence of contemporary expertise in assigned course content strong interpersonal skills. GENERAL INFORMATION : Through an innovative inter-professional education, research, and clinical practice model the High Point University Department of Athletic Training develops exceptional athletic trainers who are uniquely qualified to excel within a dynamic healthcare system.  The Department of Athletic Training emphasizes evidence-based decision making and applied research, utilizes state-of-the-art technology and novel teaching strategies, and provides unique clinical experiences to cultivate professionals who embody sound clinical reasoning, professional ethics, honesty, compassion, primacy of the patient, and are advocates for the profession of athletic training. The Department of Athletic Training is housed in the Congdon School of Health Sciences which has a state-of-the-art medical education center including a gross anatomy lab, biomechanics and physiology laboratory, and medical simulation center. The Department of Athletic Training uses three on-campus athletic training clinics plus a dedicated musculoskeletal teaching laboratory.    At High Point University the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family and country school.  High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas.  High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information or veteran status and other legally protected statuses.  The University encourages all applicants to apply.  SALARY : Competitive and commensurate with experience and qualifications.   CLOSING DATE : Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. August 2026 start date preferred but can be delayed until January 2027."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Assistant-Professor-or-Professor-of-the-Practice--Non-Tenure-Track_R0008427": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor or Professor of the Practice, Non-Tenure Track",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business Marketing Department at High Point University seeks applicants for an Assistant Professor or Professor of the Practice in Career Preparedness and Business Communications, with an anticipated start date of August 2026. QUALIFICATIONS: Education A master’s degree/doctorate in communications, an MBA, or similar degree in a related field. Experience and Training Work experience in a business setting. University-level teaching experience is required Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Applicants must have a commitment to the development of the undergraduate student’s career preparation and professionalism growth, quality teaching, personal professional growth, and university service. Must be qualified through work experience or teaching experience to teach career development and sections of BUA 2990 Business Communications as needed. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   Teaching, Student Advising, Course Administration (grading, performance monitoring, and reporting), and Student Counseling Department/School/University committee duties as assigned ACCOUNTABILITY: Prepare, deliver, and administer university-level courses as directed by the Chair Process: A review of applications will begin in mid-February and continue until the position is filled.  All applications must be submitted here in order to be considered. High Point University does not currently sponsor H-1 B visa applications for this position. For more information regarding this position, please contact Ms. Lillian Watson at lwatson@highpoint.edu"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank--Non-Tenure-Track--Tenure-Track--or-Tenured-Faculty-Member-in-the-School-of-Law_R0005846": {
      "title": "Open-Rank, Non-Tenure Track, Tenure-Track, or Tenured Faculty Member, Criminal Law or Business-Related Courses",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Kenneth F. Kahn School of Law at High Point University is seeking applicants to serve on its full-time faculty who are interested in teaching criminal law and/or business-related courses. The School invites applicants from entry-level to those seeking a tenured appointment. Entry-level candidates need not have any prior law school teaching experience but must show significant promise for excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. The School encourages applications from all candidates who will contribute to the school’s stimulating intellectual environment. Salary and academic rank will be commensurate with each candidate’s qualifications and experience. Candidates will have the exciting opportunity to work in a highly collaborative environment with a holistic approach to legal education that focuses on the doctrinal knowledge, practical skills, and values-based professional identity students need for success in a rapidly evolving legal profession. Candidates should have a passion for teaching, scholarship, and service, and should possess an entrepreneurial spirit and be well-suited to work in a collegial and student-oriented culture. In addition to teaching courses in the School of Law, faculty responsibilities will include (1) contributing to the scholarly mission of the School; (2) advising and mentoring students; and (3) participating in law school and University service as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Juris Doctor from an ABA-approved law school Exemplary academic record Successful completion of the bar exam in at least one U.S. state Demonstrated interest in teaching and student mentorship and in creating an inspiring, welcoming, and dynamic learning environment for all students Clear commitment to legal scholarship Excellent interpersonal skills sufficient to work effectively with other law school faculty and staff Willingness to contribute actively to the mission, vision, and objectives of the School and University Preferred Qualifications: Relevant experience in the practice of law or in a related professional field Prior teaching experience at a law school or graduate school. Record of scholarly publications and presentations that contribute to the improvement of the law, legal education, and/or the legal profession Active engagement is with professional organizations, such as discipline-specific organizations and bar associations Application Process: Applicants must submit the following in a single document: Their curriculum vitae with a complete professional and academic history. A letter of interest detailing the course(s) you are interested in teaching and any prior teaching experience. Names and contact information of three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, so interested individuals are encouraged to apply as soon as possible. For more information regarding this position, please contact Natt Gantt, Professor of Law and chair of the law school’s faculty appointments committee, at ngantt@ highpoint.edu. Additional Information on High Point University At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country institution, and these values are infused throughout its educational model and environment. High Point University is located in the Piedmont Triad region of North Carolina. Together, the cities of High Point, Greensboro, and Winston-Salem form the Piedmont Triad, a metropolitan area with a population of 1.9 million. The Piedmont Triad is a dynamic market that is poised for tremendous growth. Contributing factors are its temperate climate, centralized location affording quick access to major metros, relatively low population density, high quality of life, high education index, and the development of markets to leverage its manufacturing experience. U.S. News & World Report has ranked High Point University the No. 1 Best Regional College in the South for 11 consecutive years and the No. 1 Most Innovative Regional College in the South for eight consecutive years. The Princeton Review named HPU in the 2023 edition of “The Best 388 Colleges” and on the Best Southeastern Colleges “2023 Best Colleges: Region by Region” list. HPU was also recognized among the Top 20 in the nation for Best-Run Colleges, Best Career Services, Most Beautiful Campus, Most Active Student Government Association, Best College Dorms and Best Campus Food, as well as a Great School for Business/Finance Majors and a Great School for Communication Majors. For 12 years in a row, HPU has been named a College of Distinction with special recognition for career development, business and education programs. The university has 66 undergraduate majors, 68 undergraduate minors and 17 graduate degree programs. It is a member of the NCAA, Division I and the Big South Conference. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas. High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information or veteran status and other legally protected statuses. High Point University School of Law necessarily adheres to the theme of the University to which it is a constituent part to the extent these policies are protected by the United States Constitution."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank-Clinical-Faculty-Position--Law_R0008484": {
      "title": "Open Rank Clinical Faculty Position, Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Kenneth F. Kahn School of Law at High Point University School of Law invites applicants to serve as an open rank Clinical Professor of Law to begin in the Fall 2026 semester, or earlier. We are seeking a dynamic, entrepreneurial attorney to join our clinical faculty. The selected candidate will have the exciting opportunity, under the supervision of the Dean, to design and implement a new in-house clinic at the law school, with the specific subject-matter focus of the clinic to be proposed by the applicant. The selected candidate will work in a highly collaborative environment that fosters critical analysis, reasoned argument, and the free exchange of ideas and equips students with the doctrinal knowledge, practical skills, and professional values needed for success in a rapidly evolving legal profession. Candidates should be well-suited to work in a collegial and student-oriented culture. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: A J.D. degree from an ABA-approved law school and excellent academic credentials. Certifications/ Licensure: Admission to the North Carolina State Bar, or eligibility and willingness to sit for the North Carolina Bar Examination. Experience and Training: We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in a wide variety of fields, including but not limited to: Elder Law Access to Healthcare Social Security Disability Technology & Intellectual Property Criminal Defense Transactional/Entrepreneurship Law Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Significant practice experience (typically 5+ years preferred) in the area of proposed focus. Demonstrated potential for or experience in clinical teaching and supervision of students. A commitment to public service, social justice, and client-centered representation. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   This position provides a unique opportunity to design and direct a new, innovative law clinic. The successful candidate will be responsible for: Clinic Development:  Designing and implementing a new in-house clinic that provides high-quality legal services to clients while offering rich educational opportunities for law students. Supervise Students : Mentoring and supervising student attorneys in direct, live-client representation, including case selection, litigation, negotiation, or policy advocacy. Teach Seminar : Developing and teaching a seminar component that educates students by integrating substantive law with practical skills, ethics, and critical theory. Foster Partnerships : Building and maintaining relationships with community partners, social service providers, medical professionals, and others to address systemic issues. ACCOUNTABILITY: Performs all job responsibilities independently Reports directly to Dean. Application Process: Please submit in a single document the following materials: 1. Curriculum Vitae (CV). 2. A letter of Interest detailing your practice experience and your proposal for the new clinic, including the proposed focus, target client base, and educational objectives for students. 3. List of three professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, so interested individuals are encouraged to apply as soon as possible. For more information regarding this position, please contact Natt Gantt, Professor of Law and chair of the law school’s faculty appointments committee, at ngantt@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Attending-Clinical-Open-Rank-Faculty--Pediatric-Dentistry_R0007817": {
      "title": "Attending Clinical Open Rank Faculty, Pediatric Dentistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAre you a compassionate, mission-driven pediatric dentist ready to transform lives through education and care? Join High Point University’s Workman School of Dental Medicine, home to one of the nation’s most advanced new dental schools and a network of cutting-edge clinical hubs throughout the Triad region. We are disrupting traditional dental education with an integrated, real-world private practice model grounded in innovation, collaboration, and purpose. This is more than a job; it is a unique opportunity to shape the future of pediatric dental education and deliver care in an area of strong economic growth with unmet needs for specialized dental care. You will also have the opportunity to help build and potentially lead our future Pediatric Dentistry Residency Program. POSITION SUMMARY:    HPU Health- Oral Health Network is a dental network that provides primary and specialty oral health care services, part of the High Point University Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM).  This is a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure track faculty appointment with duties in the High Point University Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which includes the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs such as Advanced Education in General Dentistry, Digital Dentistry Fellowship, and Oral Oncology Fellowship. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at the time of hiring.   We are seeking a full-time Pediatric Dentist to serve in clinical and academic roles, educating future dentists while shaping pediatric protocols across our facilities. QUALIFICATIONS:   Education   DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent), active full dental licensure in the state of North Carolina (or eligible for North Carolina dental licensure) Completion of a CODA-accredited pediatric dentistry program in the US.  Licensures/ Certifications Board-certified or board-eligible in Pediatric Dentistry required Experience and Training   5 years of experience in clinical practice of dentistry is preferred. Leadership experience and program building is preferrable.  Proficiency in providing pediatric dental care in an ambulatory, inpatient, operating room, and urgent care setting.  Demonstrated passion for treatment and clinical supervision. Strong interest in residency program development is highly encouraged. Knowledge, Skills, Ability:   Robust verbal and written communication skills   Exceptional receptiveness and approachability   Poised and professional representation of HPU WSDM  Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU WSDM’s core values and mission   Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data  Clinical documentation, diagnosis, and treatment planning using electronic health records (EHR) such as EPIC systems.  Travel to oral health network sites  Developing affiliations with associated healthcare systems (children’s hospitals)  Adaptability   Integrity and innovation  Trustworthy  ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :     The candidate selected for this position will perform all duties directed by the Dean, the Director of Pediatric Dentistry, and the executive leadership team (ELT). We are seeking a full-time Pediatric Dentist to serve in clinical and potential academic roles, educating future dentists while shaping pediatric protocols across our facilities. The candidate will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to:  Patient Care : Help address a major gap in pediatric oral health in the Triad region. You will serve the community by treating patients in world class offices and hubs, ensuring high-quality and compassionate outcomes. Teach and Mentor : Deliver and teach clinical instruction in pediatric dentistry to predoctoral students and AEGD residents. Develop a Residency Pathway : Play an integral role in designing and launching a Pediatric Dentistry Residency Program, with potential to serve as Program Director. Interdisciplinary Collaboration : Work alongside top-tier faculty in orthodontics, oral and maxillofacial surgery, oral medicine, prosthodontics, and more to provide coordinated care. Model CARE Curriculum : Champion our CARE model— C ompassion, A dvocacy, R esponsibility, E xcellence—in every teaching and patient interaction. Core Values : Compassion, Integrity, Collaboration, Growth mindset, Leadership Quality Assurance    Implementation of quality improvement (QI) measures across the Pediatric Dentistry program to ensure the highest level of patient care and student learning is always provided. Utilizing proactive approaches to mitigate errors and root cause analysis to reduce errors. Frequent travel to practice sites to ensure faculty and resident experiences are met.  Accreditation    Developing the pediatric dental practice at the Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM). Ensure all standards required by the Commission of Dental Accreditation (CODA). This includes preparation for internal program audit (mock visits) and ensuring compliance of all practice sites within the oral health network.  Education   Assist in the development of the pre-doc curriculum, faculty calibration, evidence-based care guidelines, continuing education, and teaching pre-doctoral students in accordance with the needs of the Assistant Dean of Curriculum and Innovation.  True potential to create or assist in the foundation of a residency curriculum. Accountability:   Chief Dental Officer, Dean, Director of Pediatric Dentistry Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews are conducted along with an annual assessment by the CDO and include input from the faculty and students.    OUR FACILITIES & MODEL Brand-New Dental School: Featuring a world-class simulation lab, advanced clinical operatories, and integrated digital classrooms. State-of-the-Art Clinical Hubs: Located in Greensboro, Winston-Salem, and High Point—each outfitted with cutting-edge technology. Disruptive Curriculum: Our CARE-based model combines immersive education with real-world clinical training from day one. WHAT WE OFFER Competitive salary and full benefits package Dedicated faculty professional development funds A leadership role in a bold academic initiative Opportunity to shape and direct a future residency program Collaboration with visionary faculty and specialists Access to premier technology and resources A meaningful role in improving community health outcomes Being coached and mentored by experts in the field of pediatric dentistry. WHY HIGH POINT? Located in the heart of the rapidly growing Triad region, High Point offers a family-friendly lifestyle, vibrant community culture, and a unique opportunity to fill a critical gap in pediatric dental care while mentoring the next generation of clinicians. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Marc Adelberg, Clinical Associate Professor, and be sure to submit your CV and a statement of interest to: madelber@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Instructor--English_R0006811": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, English",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHigh Point University invites applications for a 9-month, nontenure-track Assistant Professor of English. The position begins August 2026. All High Point University faculty at this rank teach a 3/3 load, maintain a robust research and/or creative publishing agenda, and enjoy professional development funding as well as service opportunities to make a significant impact on the institution’s academic life. The HPU English Department comprises a collegial group of faculty representing Literature, Creative Writing, and Public and Professional Writing, who regularly teach general education courses as well as courses in their area of specialization. The successful candidate will teach courses across our writing programs and will possess expertise and previous work experience in literary, creative, and/or professional publishing. Ideally, this will allow them to teach a range of courses, including creative writing, digital editing and publishing for professional publications and develop a vision for the public and professional writing minor. Candidates who have records of scholarship related to literary, creative, and/or professional publishing are particularly encouraged to apply. Candidates should also demonstrate an understanding of GenAI's implications for writing, editing, and publishing as well as mindfulness and agility when orienting to its use instructionally. The English Department is dedicated to excellence in research, teaching, and community engagement. We welcome applications from scholars with a wide range of experiences, perspectives, and academic interests. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people. High Point University is founded in the Methodist tradition and includes students, staff, and faculty of various backgrounds, beliefs, and traditions. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas. Minimum Requirements : Terminal degree in Rhetoric and Composition, Writing Studies, Publishing Studies, or a closely related field in hand by August 2026.    Application instructions : Initial screening of applications will begin November 21, but the position will remain open until filled.  We request that applicants submit a cover letter and CV. After initial review, selected candidates will be contacted for an interview. At which point, candidates may also be asked for additional documents such as a teaching portfolio (which may include recent syllabi, assignments, and course evaluations) as well as a research and/or creative publishing plan.   For additional information or questions regarding this position, please contact the chair of the search committee: Dr. Justin Cook at jcook3@highpoint.edu"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank--Non-Tenure-Track--Faculty-Position---Pharmacy-Clinical-Sciences--Fred-Wilson-School-of-Pharmacy_R0008394": {
      "title": "Open Rank, Non-Tenure Track, Faculty Position-- Pharmacy Clinical Sciences, Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Department of Clinical Sciences in the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy at High Point University invites applications for a full-time, promotion path (non-tenure track) faculty position. The person in this position will be responsible for teaching PharmD students and providing service to the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy, the University, and the greater High Point community. This will be advanced by clinical practice collaborations maintained by the individual. The estimated effort for this individual at program maturity (i.e., when a full faculty cohort is hired) will be 50-60% teaching, 20-40% service, and 10-15% scholarship. Academic rank will be commensurate with experience. Interested candidates should apply by submitting the following documents as a single PDF file : Letter of interest addressing all qualifications for the position, including teaching philosophy and scholarship interests Current curriculum vitae Names of three current professional references with addresses, email addresses and telephone numbers For additional information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Julie Cooper, Chair and Associate Professor of Clinical Sciences at jcooper2@highpoint.edu. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) degree from an ACPE-accredited school is required Pharmacist licensure in North Carolina, or eligibility for licensure is required Experience and Training: A minimum of 1-year post-graduate training (PGY1 residency, fellowship), PhD or equivalent work experience is required.   Additional post-graduate training (e.g., PGY2 residency, fellowship) and professional certifications (BCPS) are preferred Experience relevant to the following clinical areas is preferred but not required for the position: social and administrative sciences, pharmacotherapy, internal medicine, family medicine, cardiology, emergency medicine, geriatrics, or community pharmacy. Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching and a commitment to excellence in pharmacy education and scholarship is preferred Experience working with students as a faculty mentor or preceptor is preferred   Experience or interest in applied skills-based education is preferred Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Excellent verbal and written communication and computer skills Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others Skill dealing with groups of people Develop and publish scholarly work Design and implement teaching activities that simulate contemporary pharmacy practice settings ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : Develop, coordinate, and teach content within the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy integrated curriculum as assigned by the Department Chair. Develop and offer an elective course that corresponds with expertise area(s) as needed. Utilize appropriate assessment tools and technologies to ensure effective and accurate evaluation of student learning. Provide mentorship and advisement for students in the School of Pharmacy as appointed by the Office of Student and Professional Affairs and Department Chair. Establish and maintain a clinical practice site or clinical collaborations within percent effort designated for clinical service Collaborate in the clinical environment with established pharmacists to enhance services through education, scholarship, and quality improvement initiatives. Serve as liaison between the School of Pharmacy and the faculty member’s practice site and any other collaborative associations as applicable Engage in scholarly activities, including research and dissemination of findings through publications and presentations. Integrate and enhance collaborations among the clinical sciences and basic sciences in areas of scholarship, education, and service. Advance the service missions of the School of Pharmacy and High Point University to meet community needs. Act as a representative and advocate for the department and School, both within the University and externally. Participate in committees within the Department, School of Pharmacy, and University as appointed by the Department Chair and/or Dean Participate in professional and governmental organizations. Abide by University and School of Pharmacy policies. Undertake other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair and Dean. ACCOUNTABILITY: Excellence in teaching, scholarship and service"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Oral-Medicine--Clinical-Assistant-Professor--Non--tenure-track_R0008314-1": {
      "title": "Oral Medicine/ Clinical Assistant Professor, Non- tenure track",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary This is a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure track faculty appointment with duties in the High Point University Oral Health Network (OHN) and Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which includes the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. The faculty member in Oral Medicine is responsible in providing patient care in OHN and educating pre-doctoral dental students and post-doctoral residents in WSDM. The position will report to the Chief of Hospital Programs and Clinical Development and executive leadership team (ELT) of the Workman School of Dental Medicine. Job Description ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   The candidate will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to: Patient care Provide comprehensive and emergency oral medicine, oncology, and hospital dentistry services for patients seen in affiliate hospitals with the HPU Oral Health Network (OHN) Demonstrate the highest level of professionalism, ethical-fitness, and patient-centered approach Documentation of patient history, examination findings, diagnosis, treatment planning utilizing electronic health record (EPIC) Comfort with multi-disciplinary approach to treatments Be able to cover for other OHN providers, as needed. Education Serve as an attending clinical faculty for DMD and/or residents. Involvement in curriculum design for DMD and post-doctoral students. Provide continuing education courses in HPU WSDM as a content matter expert. Serve as a clinician role model for learners and be able to thrive in a start-up education model. Leadership Developing and growing hospital service lines by establishing collaborations with other healthcare providers, administrators, and APPs Interest in hospital/GME-funded program development ACCOUNTABILITY: Chief Clinical Officer, Dean Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews is conducted along with an annual assessment by the CCO and includes input from the faculty and students. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Iquebal Hasan at ihasan@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Open-Rank-Faculty-position-and-Executive-Director-of-Women-s-Leadership_R0008302": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty position and Executive Director of Women’s Leadership",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe High Point University Women’s Leadership program is a cornerstone initiative designed to equip female students with leadership skills, mentorship, resources and industry connections to facilitate their leadership development and future success. The Executive Director of High Point University’s Women’s Leadership will lead the management, development, and delivery of courses and programmatic offerings for female students at High Point University. These include: Management, development, and delivery of programmatic offerings for the Leading and Inspiring Female Trailblazers (L.I.F.T.) Fellowship, and the Sompo Women in Insurance (S.W.I.M) Fellowship; and Management, development, and implementation of courses for the Women’s Leadership Development Minor. All programs are housed in the David S. Congdon School of Entrepreneurship (CSE). This is a faculty position requiring hands-on leadership, teaching, strategic management and mentoring skills to continue the delivery of excellent educational experiences for HPU’s top female students. As one of our most prestigious scholars’ programs, the L.I.F.T. Fellowship provides students with experiential learning opportunities that further their leadership skills. The successful candidate will be qualified to teach women’s leadership studies courses, develop meaningful programming for L.I.F.T. Fellows, mentor students and lead a team of two faculty and one staff member who support students through their four-year term at High Point University. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Strategic Leadership Develop and implement multi-year strategic plans for: L.I.F.T. and SOMPO Women in Insurance Management (SWIM) Fellows programming, including budgets, clear objectives, milestones and measures of success. Strickland Women’s Leadership Council (SWLC) engagement and governance. Lead the design and execution of programs that foster women’s leadership development, including mentorship programs, workshops, community engagement events and the SWLC engagement. Build and maintain partnerships with faculty, internal and external mentors, alumni, and SWLC members to support student growth and engagement. Develop, design and deliver academic courses the deliver leadership learnings. Achieve and deliver on the mission and goals of High Point University and the Congdon School of Entrepreneurship, aligning with School and University priorities Program Leadership & Management Oversee daily program operations, budgets and performance reporting while ensuring the effective use of resources and space. Including, but not limited to: Student recruitment, including attending Admissions Events, Open Houses, student applicant outreach, L.I.F.T./SWIM/SWLC activities, etc. Admissions management, including student application development, review, scoring and notifications. Student retention through intentional engagement opportunities, cohort activities (including the annual third year cohort trip), and individualized one-on-one mentorship of Fellows in the program. Plan and direct, with internal and external partners. L.I.F.T. Co-Directors and the Women’s Leadership Program Associate, seven annual events. Establish monitoring methods to track metrics and satisfaction scores to promote student outcomes and program impact. Represent L.I.F.T./SWIM within the university and externally, acting as the champion of women’s leadership development. Lead and manage faculty co-directors and Women’s Leadership Program Associate. Teaching Provide high-quality instruction in leadership, focusing on women’s leadership development, including lectures and experiential learning opportunities. Including: L.I.F.T. Fellowship courses Courses associated with the Women’s Leadership Development (WLD) minor Management of the WLD Minor and related courses and faculty Engage in service activities within the school and university. Collaborate with faculty members across departments and schools to enhance interdisciplinary learning. Student Support Serve as the primary point of contact for participating L.I.F.T./SWIM Fellows. Plan and facilitate workshops, webinars, and networking events. Facilitate connections between students, SWLC, and mentors.   Provide mentor and advisor role to student participants, as needed. Partnership & Stakeholder Engagement Cultivate, build and maintain partner relationships with mentors, industry experts, and SWLC to support student engagement and growth. Collaborate with internal HPU/CSE teams to enhance program visibility and integration. Partner with Institutional Advancement to host the annual Strickland Women’s Leadership Summit and Strickland Trailblazer Awards Cultivate and maintain partnerships with Sompo Insurance and the (SWIM) Program. Communicate and provide regular and ongoing updates with Fellows, mentors, and internal and external stakeholders Alumni Engagement Cultivate and maintain alumni engagement programming and relationships with HPU and L.I.F.T. graduates. Partner with Institutional Advancement on ways to integrate this group with existing programming while also creating new opportunities to strengthen the network for alumni and current students’ benefit. Establish a resource and support network with L.I.F.T. graduates and Strickland Trailblazer Award finalists and recipients Qualifications: Advanced degree in business, leadership development, education, or a related field preferred. (PhD in Leadership Development or other leadership studies preferred) Strong leadership, organizational, and communication skills with demonstrated ability to work collaboratively across complex organizations. This includes, but is not limited to, exceptional interpersonal communication, project and stakeholder management, and relationship-building skills. Significant experience in leadership development, education, and mentor management, with a proven track record of teaching and program management. Experience working in a higher education environment is highly desirable. Experience working with volunteer boards/councils and/or high net worth individuals is highly desirable. Passion for student development, mentorship, internal and external stakeholder management and community building. The successful candidate may come to this position from many different backgrounds including one of the following: Demonstrated success in partnership development and network engagement, ideally in a higher education or nonprofit context. Experience leading leadership programs or centers, with a track record of advancing student/participant outcomes and/or strategic goals. Experience in developing experiential learning opportunities and integration of leadership training in a university setting, preferred. Reporting : The Executive Director will report to the Dean of the Congdon School of Entrepreneurship, with additional reporting responsibilities to the Provost’s Office. About this program : The L.I.F.T Fellowship Program provides networking, leadership development, mentorship and coaching for students interested in becoming CEOs, leaders, entrepreneurs, executives, and trailblazers in their chosen careers. The program is not limited to any one field of study. Rather, L.I.F.T. students will work alongside accomplished faculty and executives to strengthen their self-efficacy, confidence, and leadership capacity. It is anticipated that the L.I.F.T. Fellowship Program will generate a sustainable pipeline of students who desire to blaze a trail for themselves as they progress in college and into the next stages of their lives. An additional opportunity is provided to four students annually to participate in the SWIM Fellowship which provides mentorship, internships, and possible job placement at SOMPO Insurance. The L.I.F.T. Fellowship is made possible through the vision and generosity of Elizabeth Miller Strickland. A trailblazer herself, Strickland attended HPU where she was crowned Miss High Point College in 1952. Betty and her late husband Bob, former chairman of the board of Lowe’s Home Improvement, believed in education, mentorship, experiential learning and the God, family, and country values that HPU embodies. This position has responsibility for: The Women's L.I.F.T. ( Leading & Inspiring Female Trailblazers ) Fellowship, Sompo Women in Insurance Management (SWIM) Program, and Women’s Leadership Development Minor Learn more: https://www.highpoint.edu/admissions/strickland-womens-lift-fellowship/"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Chemistry_R0008190": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Chemistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-12-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Wanek School of Natural Sciences at High Point University is currently seeking an Adjunct Instructor of Chemistry. The Adjunct In structor will have the opportunity to teach general chemistry laboratory courses emphasiz in g critical th in k in g skills and proper laboratory techniques in the general chemistry curriculum.   The selected candidate will be responsible for the delivery of a pre-lab lecture emphasiz in g safety for that day’s lab, timely grad in g of assignments, and post in g grades through our onl in e course management software.  A Master's degree or equ ivalent in chemistry or a related field is r equ ired .     For more in formation regard in g this position please contact Dr. Todd Knippenberg, Chair and Associate Professor at mknippen@highpo in t.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Attending-Faculty--OMFS-and-Anesthesiology--Clinical--Open-Rank--Full-time-_R0008202": {
      "title": "Attending Faculty, OMFS and Anesthesiology, Clinical (Open Rank, Full-time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-11-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Workman School of Dental Medicine is currently seeking an Attending Faculty position. This is a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure track faculty appointment with duties in the High Point University Oral Health Network (OHN) and Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which includes the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. The faculty member in Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery and Dental Anesthesiology is responsible in providing patient care in OHN and educating pre-doctoral dental students and post-doctoral residents in WSDM. The position will report to the Chief Dental Officer and executive leadership team (ELT) of the Workman School of Dental Medicine. QUALIFICATIONS: Education DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent), active full dental licensure in the state of North Carolina MD degree is preferred, but not required Completion of a CODA-accredited Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery residency program in the United Stated Experience and Training 5 years of experience in OMFS practice and/or teaching is preferred, but not required. Experience in hospital-based and private-practice (outpatient) environments Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Robust verbal and written communication skills Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU WSDM’s core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Clinical documentation, diagnosis, and treatment planning using electronic health records (EHR) such as EPIC systems. Travel to OHN (oral health network) sites Adaptability Coachability Integrity and innovation Trustworthy ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   The candidate selected for this position will perform all duties directed by the Chief Dental Officer and WSDM executive leadership team (ELT). The candidate will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to: Patient care Provide comprehensive and emergency OMFS services for patients seen in affiliate hospitals with the HPU Oral Health Network (OHN) Demonstrate the highest level of professionalism, ethical-fitness, and patient-centered approach Documentation of patient history, examination findings, diagnosis, treatment planning utilizing electronic health record (EPIC) Comfort with multi-disciplinary approach to treatments Be able to cover for other OHN providers, as needed. Education Serve as an attending clinical faculty for DMD and/or residents. Involvement in curriculum design for DMD and post-doctoral students. Provide continuing education courses in HPU WSDM as a content matter expert. Serve as a clinician role model for learners and be able to thrive in a start-up education model. Leadership Developing and growing hospital service lines by establishing collaborations with other healthcare providers, administrators, and APPs Interest in hospital/GME-funded program development in dental anesthesiology and potentially OMFS Provide feedback for design and development of surgical/specialty HUBs ACCOUNTABILITY: Chief Dental Officer, Dean Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews is conducted along with an annual assessment by the CDO and includes input from the ELT, faculty and students. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Thomas Roth, Clinical Associate Professor and Interim Chief Dental Officer at troth@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Greensboro-Hub/Associate-Professor-of-Care-Convergence--Applied-Research-and-Entrepreneurship--CCARE-_R0008097": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Care Convergence: Applied Research and Entrepreneurship (C.C.A.R.E.)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-10-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Associate Professor of Care Convergence: Applied Research and Entrepreneurship (C.C.A.R.E.) is a part-time, non-tenure track faculty appointment. This role is designed to advance the Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM) as a leader in the field of integrated medical-dental care. The objective of this role is to foster next-generation care delivery through a focus on medical-dental integration, tech-enabled operations, and data-driven performance management. The role will closely liaise with the Dean, faculty, and staff to build upon existing strategies, research, and educational initiatives that highlight the convergence of medical and dental care with technology and position WSDM as the leader in this field. This position works closely with Dean of WSDM, Dr. Muhammad Ali Shazib, the Senior Associate Dean for Administration and Finance, Dr. Kevin Cain and Executive Leadership Team (ELT), to develop relevant curriculum, research, partnerships, processes and procedures that advance integrated care delivery models and encourage the development and deployment of relevant IP and solutions by students, faculty and staff. Efforts of this role are focused on ensuring industry-shaping through leadership, clinical operations and entrepreneurial ecosystem where innovators can thrive. The Professor of C.C.A.R.E will play an integral role in ecosystem development, tech transfer, research and entrepreneurship. QUALIFICATIONS: Education A Master’s degree or higher in Business, Healthcare Administration, or a related field is required. Advanced training or experience in medical-dental integration, healthcare innovation, or technology adoption is required. Experience and Training 15+ years of executive experience, preferably at a Fortune 20 company, with proven leadership in medical-dental integration, healthcare technology, or healthcare innovation. Demonstrated success in building and scaling tech-enabled solutions across health disciplines, including leadership of cross-functional teams and academic research. Track record of thought leadership in medical dental integration, entrepreneurship and exponential technologies Experience in developing and managing high-profile partnerships with industry leaders, universities, or healthcare organizations. Expertise in healthcare data interoperability, strategic planning, and the implementation of data-driven performance metrics and key performance indicators (KPIs). Strong background in entrepreneurship, with experience advising or investing in healthcare startups, and mentoring students or professionals in innovation and leadership. Experience in creating and leading training programs focused on AI, technology adoption, and healthcare transformation. Firsthand experience as operator – entrepreneur as well as leading and building teams in large organizations Extensive meaningful network of strategic players in healthcare delivery, payments and life sciences Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Exceptional verbal and written communication skills with the ability to lead and mentor cross-disciplinary teams. Strong strategic and analytical thinking skills with a focus on technology adoption, impact entrepreneurship, and systemic health innovation. Ability to translate complex healthcare concepts into actionable teaching materials and practical frameworks for students and professionals. Extensive knowledge of emerging trends in healthcare delivery, medical-dental integration, and data-driven decision-making models. Experience in publishing research and thought leadership in areas such as healthcare innovation, systemic health, and tech-enabled care convergence. Proven track record of hands-on leadership and self-starter mindset Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM/Health Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU WSDM’S core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Track record of building ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   The candidate selected for this position will perform all duties directed by the Dean, with input from the leadership team. The candidate will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to: 1. Curriculum Development: Design and deliver courses that highlight interprofessional collaboration, business fundamentals, technology adoption, leadership, and entrepreneurship. Incorporate key topics such as technology literacy, integrated care models, and managing ambiguity in the existing curriculum as relevant. 2. Research and Thought Leadership: Conduct research and publish insights on care convergence models, contributing to the future Care Convergence Center at WSDM. Establish WSDM as a leader in integrated care delivery through industry-leading publications and partnerships with the entrepreneurial ecosystem. 3. Integrated Care Delivery: Develop and implement patient, and care team journeys for the dental clinics operated by WSDM, focusing on operational efficiency, patient-centered care, and clinical excellence. Establish KPIs and agile feedback mechanisms for continuous improvement and data-driven decision-making. 4. Strategic Initiatives: Collaborate with the Dean, faculty, and staff to: Develop applied care convergence models and advance the school's strategy in medical-dental integration. Establish a technology transfer office (Care Convergence Center) as part of WSDM’s intellectual property (IP) strategy. Set up a dental clinical research organization designed to validate innovative solutions advancing care convergence Leadership and Mentorship: Mentor students and faculty in the areas of leadership, entrepreneurship, and applied clinical practices, fostering an environment of innovation and impact. ACCOUNTABILITY: Dean, Workman School of Dental Medicine, with input from the leadership team Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews is conducted along with an annual assessment by the Dean and includes input from the faculty and students."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Greensboro-Hub/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Oral-and-Maxillofacial-Surgery---Dental-Anesthesiology-and-Medical-Director-of-OHN-Surgical-Specialty-Services_R0008066": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery & Dental Anesthesiology and Medical Director of OHN Surgical/Specialty Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-09-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHPU Health – Oral Health Network (OHN) is a non-profit dental network that delivers comprehensive primary and specialty/surgical oral health care in affiliation with the High Point University Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM). This is a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure track faculty appointment as Assistant/Associate Professor of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery & Dental Anesthesiology and Medical Director of OHN Surgical/Specialty Services. Professional rank will be commensurate with experience and qualifications at the time of hire. The faculty member and Medical Director will provide direct patient care, educate pre-doctoral students and post-doctoral residents, and serve in a leadership capacity to support the clinical quality, safety, and growth of OHN’s surgical and specialty programs. This position reports to the Chief Dental Officer (CDO) and the WSDM Executive Leadership Team (ELT). QUALIFICATIONS Education DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent) and active, unrestricted dental licensure in North Carolina Completion of a CODA-accredited Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery residency program in the United States MD degree preferred, but not required Experience and Training Minimum 5 years of practice and/or teaching experience in Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery preferred (not required) Experience in hospital-based and outpatient/private-practice environments Prior leadership, directorship, or program-building experience desirable Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent verbal and written communication skills Professional presence with strong interpersonal skills and approachability Receptive to feedback, continuous improvement, and coaching Strong alignment with HPU WSDM’s mission and core values Ability to articulate clinical, operational, and analytical concepts clearly Proficiency in electronic health records (EHR), preferably EPIC Demonstrated leadership skills in program oversight, quality improvement, and interprofessional collaboration Willingness to travel across OHN practice sites Attributes: adaptability, integrity, innovation, collaboration, and trustworthiness ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Patient Care Provide comprehensive and emergency OMFS services for patients at OHN-affiliated hospitals and clinics Deliver care with professionalism, ethical responsibility, and a patient-centered approach Document history, examination findings, diagnoses, and treatment plans in EPIC Participate in multidisciplinary care and treatment planning Provide coverage for other OHN providers as needed Education Serve as attending faculty for DMD students and/or post-doctoral residents Contribute to curriculum design and development at the pre-doctoral and post-doctoral levels Provide continuing education (CE) courses in areas of expertise Act as a clinician role model, thriving in an innovative, start-up educational environment Leadership – Medical Director Functions Support the CDO and ELT in oversight of surgical and specialty services within OHN Ensure high standards of patient safety, quality assurance, and compliance across specialty programs Participate in the development of clinical protocols, infection control, and quality improvement initiatives Serve as a liaison with hospital partners on medical/clinical issues, credentialing, and privileging Mentor faculty, residents, and advanced practice providers (APPs) in clinical practice standards Provide input into the design and expansion of OHN surgical/specialty hubs and future GME-funded programs ACCOUNTABILITY Reports to: Chief Dental Officer and Dean Evaluation: Performance reviewed on an ongoing basis with annual assessments conducted by the CDO, incorporating feedback from the ELT, faculty, and students"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Mechanical-Engineering--Non-tenure-Track_R0007906": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-09-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Engineering at High Point University seeks three new full-time faculty at the Assistant/Associate ranks to begin August 2026. HPU launched new Mechanical Engineering and Mechatronics majors in Fall 2024 and state of the art Makerspace and teaching labs in Fall 2025. We will make multiple hires to support these rapidly growing programs. We seek creative, dynamic individuals to play a critical role in the development of innovative, active learning classes and laboratories, and to mentor highly motivated students in undergraduate research projects and design competitions. The successful candidates will teach a variety of courses within the Mechanical Engineering and Mechatronics programs. Additional expectations include academic advising, supporting undergraduate research, assisting the department with ABET accreditation, and serving on college and university-wide committees. One new hire will be enthusiastic about leading our Senior Design Project course, including developing partnerships with local industry. Faculty appointments are for a nine-month contract period with a normal teaching load of 12 credit hours per semester. QUALIFICATIONS: Education Candidates must have an earned Ph.D. or doctorate in Mechanical Engineering or Mechatronics, or a closely related field like Aerospace, Manufacturing, or Materials Science. All areas of research specialty are accepted, and industry experience is also desirable. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: The successful candidate should have demonstrated promise of excellence in teaching, a record of scholarly achievement, an entrepreneurial spirit and an interest in working with highly motivated undergraduate students. While it is anticipated that these positions will be filled at the Assistant Professor level, highly qualified applicants will be considered for higher ranks. The success of our undergraduate students is our primary focus. Responsibilities: Teach 24 contact hours (typically 5 – 6 classes) per year Advise students Produce scholarly research or creative activity, especially in partnership with undergraduate students Assist with curriculum development and ABET Accreditation Assist with university recruiting efforts Participate in department, college, and university meetings and committees Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair and/or Dean Founded in 1924, HPU is a 101-year-old liberal arts institution located in the Piedmont Triad region of North Carolina. At High Point University, every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people. “America’s Best Colleges” 2025 Edition, published in the U.S. News & World Report, ranks HPU #1 among all regional colleges in the South and #1 as Most Innovative Regional College in the South for innovative improvements in curriculum, faculty, students, campus life, technology, and facilities. All applicants must submit a single attachment with the following sections: A letter of interest addressing the required qualifications and responsibilities A current CV A statement of teaching philosophy A statement of research interests Unofficial transcripts of graduate and undergraduate education Names and contact information for three professional recommendations Any questions related to this position should be sent to Dr. Brian Bernard, Department Chair of Mechanical Engineering and Mechatronics, bbernard@highpoint.edu . Review of applications will begin September 29 and will continue until the positions are filled. Start date for each new hire is August 2026. Applicants who don’t meet the qualifications or are not legally authorized to work in the US will not be considered. Choose to be Extraordinary!"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Media-Production_R0007778": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Media Production",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-08-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Nido R. Qubein School of Communication at High Point University is seeking a part-time Adjunct Instructor to teach MPE3361 Motion Graphics 1 this Spring 2026. This course focuses on the theory and practice of motion graphic design. Students will learn to create effective, efficient, and dynamic motion graphics for use in motion pictures, broadcast media, and the web. Class time will be divided between screenings, discussions, exercises, and lab time. Qualifications:   Proficiency in Adobe After Effects, Adobe Photoshop, and Adobe Illustrator software .   Master's degree with 18 hours in the field OR Master's degree with commensurate experience .     For more information regarding this position, please contact Michelle Devlin at mdevlin@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Operations-and-Supply-Chain-Management--Undergraduate-and-or-MBA-_R0007889": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Operations and Supply Chain Management (Undergraduate and/or MBA)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-08-11\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nHigh Point University (HPU) is seeking a highly motivated and qualified individual for the position of Adjunct Instructor of Operations and Supply Chain Management for the Undergraduate and/or Master’s in Business Administration Programs. In the undergraduate program, the successful candidate will be responsible for teaching courses in Supply Chain Management, Operations Management, and related topics to undergraduate students in a face-to-face format. In the MBA program, the successful candidate will be responsible for teaching graduate courses in Supply Chain Management, Operations Management, and related topics to students in an online and asynchronous environment. Key Responsibilities Be responsible for leading courses in supply chain management, logistics and distribution, project management, operations management, inventory control, etc. Engage in high-quality research that contributes to courses taught and results in staying abreast of new thought and developments in the fields of supply chain, logistics, warehousing and distribution. Provide mentorship and academic advising to students if necessary Develop and update course materials to enhance student learning. Abide by University and School of Business policies Undertake other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair and/or the MBA Director Qualifications An earned doctoral degree (PhD or DBA) in Management, Business Administration, or a closely related field (ABD candidates will be considered) from an accredited institution is required. The candidate must have a minimum of 18 hours of graduate coursework closely related to supply chain or operations management, business management, or a related field. Teaching experience at the university level is highly preferred in addition to teaching online using various Learning Management Systems such as Blackboard specifically. Preferred Qualifications A minimum of 7 years of industry experience in the field of supply chain management, operations, and/or logistics as well as a minimum of 5 years in a senior leadership role. Experience with online and hybrid teaching modalities. Teaching experience in an accredited academic program. Application Process Interested candidates should submit:​ A cover letter highlighting qualifications and research history. Unofficial copies of all transcripts. Curriculum Vitae (CV) and or resume. Contact information for three professional references."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor-of-Clinical-Sciences---Social-Administrative-Science-and-Director-of-Programmatic-Assessment--Non---Tenure-Track_R0004764": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position, Non-tenure track, Pharmacy Clinical Sciences - Internal Medicine /Acute Care",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Department of Clinical Sciences in the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy at High Point University invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track faculty position. The person in this position will be responsible for teaching PharmD students and providing service to the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy, University, and the greater High Point community. This will be advanced by clinical practice collaborations maintained by the individual. The estimated effort for this individual at program maturity (i.e., when a full faculty cohort is hired) will be 10% research, 60-70% teaching and 20-30% service. Academic rank will be commensurate with experience. Interested candidates should apply by submitting the following documents as one single PDF file: • Letter of interest addressing all qualifications for the position • Current curriculum vitae • Statement of teaching/scholarship philosophy and research interests • Names of three current professional references with addresses, email addresses and telephone numbers For additional information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Julie Cooper, Chair and Associate Professor of Clinical Sciences at jcooper2@highpoint.edu. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) degree from an ACPE-accredited school is required Pharmacist licensure in North Carolina, or eligibility for licensure is required Experience and Training: Pharm.D. with a minimum of 1-year post-graduate training (PGY1 residency, fellowship) or equivalent work experience.   Additional post-graduate training (e.g., PGY2 residency, fellowship) and professional certifications (BCPS) are also highly preferred. Preference will be given to individuals with training in one or more of the following areas:  pharmacotherapy, internal medicine, cardiology, emergency medicine, or geriatrics. Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching and a commitment to excellence in pharmacy education and research Experience working with students as a faculty mentor or preceptor Experience with applied skills-based education is preferred Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Excellent verbal and written communication and computer skills Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others Skill in dealing with individuals in varied roles and settings Ability to write scholarly documents Ability to work with and teach using electronic medical records ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS : Develop, coordinate, and teach content within the Fred Wilson School of Pharmacy integrated curriculum as appointed by the Department Chair. Develop and offer an elective course that corresponds with expertise area(s) as needed. Provide mentorship and advisement for students in the School of Pharmacy as appointed by the Dean’s Office and Department Chair. Establish and maintain and acute care practice site within percent effort designated for practice Collaborate in the clinical environment with established pharmacists to enhance services through education, research, and quality improvement initiatives. Provide unique targeted clinical assistance when asked. Share teaching responsibilities at clerkship sites upon request. Serve as liaison between the School of Pharmacy and the faculty member’s practice site if applicable or other clinical practice collaborations. Publish scientific findings in peer-reviewed journals, produce case reports and present research findings at national and international meetings as allowed by the allocated research effort. Integrate and enhance collaborations among the clinical sciences and basic sciences in areas of research, education, and service. Advance the service missions of the School of Pharmacy and High Point University to meet community needs. Act as a representative and advocate for the department, both within the University and externally. Participate in committees within the Department, School of Pharmacy, and University and participate in professional and governmental organizations as appointed by the Department Chair. Abide by University and School of Pharmacy policies. Undertake other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair. Utilize ExamSoft® or other software to conduct all School of Pharmacy assessments. ACCOUNTABILITY: Excellence in teaching, research and service"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--MBA-Program_R0007676": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, MBA Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-06-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business at High Point University is seeking part-time Adjunct Instructors for our online asynchronous MBA program in the following disciplines: Accounting, Business Analytics, Economics, Finance, Healthcare Management, Management, Marketing, Sales, and Supply Chain Management. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed in our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. To learn more about our MBA program, please visit our website: https://www.highpoint.edu/graduate/master-of-business-administration/ For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Nasir Assar, Director of the MBA Program at nassar@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: Ph.D. or a DBA in the teaching discipline. Please upload a copy of your CV or resume. Also upload an unofficial copy of your Ph.D. or DBA transcript.  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  This will be used to verify that you have at least 18 graduate semester hours in the teaching discipline. Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ).  Be sure this is clearly stated on your CV or resume. Provide a list of references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate online teaching experience is preferred but not required. If you have other relevant qualifications, make sure they are clearly stated in your cover letter.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches the subjects at the collegiate level. The ability to conduct and prepare curriculum for an online asynchronous environment. Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Street-Hub/Clinical-Associate-Professor--Oral-and-Maxillofacial-Pathology_R0007561": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate Professor; Oral and Maxillofacial Pathology",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-06-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThis is a part-time, non-tenure track faculty appointment with duties in the High Point University Oral Health Network (OHN) and Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which includes the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. The faculty member in Oral and Maxillofacial Pathology is responsible for developing curriculum content and instructional elements for the pre-doctoral dental students and post-doctoral residents in WSDM. The position will report to the executive leadership team (ELT) of the Workman School of Dental Medicine through the Assistant Dean for Education. QUALIFICATIONS: Education DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent), eligibility for dental licensure (instructor) in the state of North Carolina Completion of a CODA-accredited or equivalent foreign program in oral and maxillofacial pathology Experience and Training Preferably board-eligible from the American Board of Oral and Maxillofacial Pathology 5 years of experience in clinical practice of dentistry is preferred, but not required. Experience in teaching pre-doctoral and post-doctoral learners through case-based learning Experience in dental education is preferred, but not required. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Robust verbal and written communication skills Highly developed critical thinking skills Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU WSDM’s core values and mission Commitment to and exemplary embodiment of core values of compassion, innovation, growth mindset, learning and leadership, integrity and trust. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   The candidate selected for this position will perform all duties directed by the Assistant Dean for Education and WSDM executive leadership team (ELT). The candidate will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to: Education Support curriculum content design and delivery in classroom-based and simulation-based learning environments for DMD and post-doctoral programs. Provide continuing education (CE) courses in HPU WSDM as a content matter expert. Delivery of content through asynchronous, hybrid, or on-site methods of instruction. ACCOUNTABILITY: Assistant Dean for Education, with input from the Executive Leadership Team Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews is conducted along with an annual assessment by ELT and input from the faculty and students. For further information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Kristin Ackerman, Associate Professor and Chief Discovery Officer, via email at kackerma@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Associate-Professor--Founding-Program-Director--Pediatric-Dentistry_R0007633": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/ Founding Program Director, Pediatric Dentistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-06-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis is a full-time, 12-month, non-tenure track faculty appointment with duties in the High Point University Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which includes the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs such as pediatric dentistry. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. The Founding Director for Pediatric Dentistry is responsible for developing the pediatric dentistry residency program, faculty recruitment, supervision of residents, providing patient care, and pre-doctoral pediatric dentistry. The program director will be responsible for achieving accreditation by the Commission of Dental Accreditation (CODA) standards. This is a unique leadership opportunity to build programs and work closely with the executive leadership team (ELT). The position will report to the executive leadership team (ELT) of the Workman School of Dental Medicine. QUALIFICATIONS: Education DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent), active full dental licensure in the state of North Carolina Completion of a CODA-accredited pediatric dentistry program in the US. Must be certified by the American Board of Pediatric Dentistry. Experience and Training 5 years of experience in clinical practice of dentistry Leadership experience and program building is preferable. Proficiency in providing pediatric dental care in an ambulatory, inpatient, operating room and urgent care setting. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Robust verbal and written communication skills Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU SDMOH’s core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Clinical documentation, diagnosis, and treatment planning using electronic health records (EHR) such as EPIC systems. Travel to oral health network sites Developing affiliations with associated healthcare systems (children’s hospitals) Adaptability Coachability Integrity and innovation Trustworthy ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   The candidate selected for this position will perform all duties directed by the Dean of the WSDM and executive leadership team (ELT). The candidate will be expected to perform the following duties, including but not limited to: Pediatric Dentistry program development Familiarity with and management of all program-related documents and reporting platforms including, but not limited to, resident employment, resident attendance, faculty onboarding, resident licensure, resident requirements, resident and program outcomes, resident certification, and GME-related and program-related policies. Oversight and monitoring of all program-related evaluations and reporting. Orientation of new residents and faculty. Point-of-contact person for any issues related to the Pediatric Dentistry program. Quality Assurance Implementation of quality improvement (QI) measures across the Pediatric Dentistry program to ensure highest level of patient care and residency learning are being always provided. Utilizing proactive approaches to mitigate errors and root cause analysis to reduce errors. Frequent travel to practice sites to ensure faculty and resident experiences are being met. Accreditation In addition to developing the inaugural Pediatric Dentistry program at Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM), the founding program director will ensure that it meets all standards required by the Commission of Dental Accreditation (CODA). This includes preparation for internal program audit (mock visits) and ensuring compliance of all practice sites within the oral health network. During the program accreditation process, the individual will be expected to see pediatric dental patients. Education Development of residency curriculum, faculty calibration, evidence-based care guidelines, continuing education, and teaching pre-doctoral students in accordance with the needs of the Assistant Dean of Curriculum and Innovation. ACCOUNTABILITY: Chief Clinical Officer, Dean Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews is conducted along with an annual assessment by the CCO and includes input from the faculty and students. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Muhammad Ali Shazib, Associate Professor and Chief Clinical Officer, HPU Oral Health System at mshazib@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Spanish_R0007500": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Spanish",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-06-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Department of World Languages, Literatures, and Cultures at High Point University is seeking an Adjunct Instructor of Spanish to begin in August 2025. The successful candidate will hold a master’s degree in Spanish, possess native or near-native proficiency in both Spanish and English, demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching excellence, and show interest in teaching a full range of language courses within the curriculum. Applicants should send 1. Letter of application; 2. Current Curriculum vitae; 3. Statement of teaching philosophy; 4. Contact information for three references. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Hayden Carron at hcarron@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Italian_R0007386": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Italian",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Department of World Languages, Literatures, & Cultures at High Point University is accepting applications for adjunct instructors to teach introductory courses in Italian starting from August 2025. Responsibilities include course preparation, meeting with students during office hours, and communicating with students outside of class via Blackboard, email, or telephone. Qualifications Education: A master's degree in Italian language, literature, teaching, or a related field Near-native fluency in English and Italian Experience/Training: College-level teaching experience is required. Preference will be given to candidates with experience using technology in and out of the classroom and a student-centered, communicative-based teaching philosophy. Evidence of successful teaching is also desirable. To apply, please submit your CV, including contact information for three references, along with a one-page application letter on the university website. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Daliang Wang at dwang@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Finance_R0004127": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Finance",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-03-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business at High Point University is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Finance. We are looking to fill sections of Finance courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Ross Roberts, Chair and Associate Professor, Accounting at rroberts@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: Ph.D. in the teaching discipline preferred; a master’s degree and/or appropriate professional experience in the teaching discipline will be considered. Upload an unofficial copy of your Ph.D. and/or a master’s transcript.  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  This will be used to verify you have at least 18 graduate semester hours in Finance. Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). If you have less than 18 hours, we will consider your commensurate experience/training.  Be sure this is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches Finance at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas.  High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, and other legally protected statuses.  The University encourages all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Chair-of-Electrical-and-Computer-Engineering_R0007240": {
      "title": "Chair of Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-02-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nHigh Point University invites applications for the position of Chair of the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering within the Webb School of Engineering. The successful candidate will provide visionary leadership, fostering excellence in teaching, research, and service. This role includes overseeing curriculum development, faculty recruitment and development, research initiatives, and student success strategies. The Chair will also work collaboratively with other departments and the Dean to advance the mission of the School and University. Key Responsibilities: Lead the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, promoting a culture of academic excellence and innovation. Oversee curriculum development and ensure alignment with industry standards and accreditation requirements. Recruit, mentor, and evaluate faculty members, supporting their professional growth and scholarly activities. Develop and implement strategies to enhance student recruitment, retention, and success. Facilitate and promote research initiatives, encouraging faculty and student participation in scholarly activities. Manage departmental budgets and resources effectively. Cultivate partnerships with industry, government agencies, and other academic institutions to enhance educational and research opportunities. Qualifications: An earned doctorate in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or a closely related field. A distinguished record of teaching, research, and service appropriate for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor. Demonstrated leadership experience in an academic setting, including curriculum development and faculty supervision. Experience with accreditation processes and standards, particularly ABET accreditation. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to foster a collaborative and collegial environment among faculty, staff, and students. Application Process: All applicants must submit a single attachment with the following sections: A cover letter detailing their qualifications and vision for the Department. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of teaching philosophy. A statement of research interests. Unofficial transcripts of graduate and undergraduate education Name and contact information for at least three professional references. Applications must be submitted through the university’s job site: https://highpoint.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Highpoint-Faculty About High Point University: High Point University is a private liberal arts institution located in High Point, North Carolina. The University is committed to delivering educational experiences that enlighten, challenge, and prepare students to lead lives of significance in complex global communities. The Webb School of Engineering offers innovative programs designed to produce well-rounded graduates with strong technical skills and the necessary life skills to be successful engineers and computer scientists.   Any questions related to this position should be sent to Dr. Michal Oudshoorn, Dean of Engineering, moudshoo@highpoint.edu   Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants who do not meet the qualifications or are not legally authorized to work in the US will not be considered. Choose to be Extraordinary!"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Clinical-Adjunct-Instructor--BSN-program_R0007162": {
      "title": "Clinical Adjunct Instructor, BSN program",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-12-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Teresa Caine School of Nursing at High Point University invites applications for a part-time (Adjunct Instructor) nursing faculty position starting in the spring semester of 2025. The Adjunct Instructor will have a strong teaching and clinical background in Adult Health/Medical Surgical Nursing and will utilize the nursing process to teach professional nursing skills in a clinical setting under the direction of the Founding Dean, the lead course faculty, and the clinical coordinator. Responsibilities include clinical practicum instruction, clinical learning simulation exercises, documentation of students’ progress, and adherence to the Teresa Caine School of Nursing guidelines and policies along with those of the respective clinical agency. This clinical practicum focuses on adult populations with complex multisystem health conditions. Emphasis is on the prioritization and coordination of interdisciplinary care, systems-based practices, and nursing leadership during clinical judgment and decision-making processes in clinical and simulated practice environments. Assisting students with the integration of the nursing process, evidence-based practices, best practices, interdisciplinary person-centered care management, and evaluation for diverse adult populations is expected. Qualifications   Education: Minimum: Master’s degree in nursing education or equivalent from an accredited institution Educational preparation in teaching and learning principles for adult education Experience: Three or more years of clinical practice as a RN in a medical-surgical/adult health nursing practice area Familiarity with simulation education (preferably in a medical-surgical/adult health nursing practice area) Three or more years of teaching (clinical) in a higher educational program (preferably at the BSN level) Licensure: Unrestricted license as a Registered Nurse in North Carolina (or eligible) Essential Functions: BSN (adjunct) Faculty Responsibilities   Clinical instruction using evidence-based methodology  Academic mentorship and modeling of professional nursing practice   Assisting with nursing simulations    Additional duties as assigned  Essential Knowledge   Familiarity with North Carolina Board of Nursing’s Regulations and Standards  Clinical practice background in a medical-surgical nursing/adult health practice area  Familiar with education principles and standards for professional nursing practice   Fosters the development and delivery of best practices, evidence-based practices, and professional nursing practice with respect to technology and pedagogical principles  Essential Skills   Familiarity with simulation education   Three or more years of clinical nursing practice experience in an adult health/med-surg environment  CPR certified  Exceptional organizational, interpersonal, collaborative, team building, and communication skills (written and oral)  Student-centered  Demonstrated commitment in all settings  Ability To   Work as a team; good time-management skills; good interpersonal/human relations skills  Communicate effectively orally, in writing and through technology  Follow instructions as well as take initiative  Adapt to change in a progressive environment of constant change  Embrace working in an interdisciplinary atmosphere  Attend campus for orientation and clinical practicum sites for in-person instruction  For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Racquel Ingram, Founding Dean, Teresa Caine School of Nursing at ringram1@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Mechanical-and-Mechatronic-Engineering_R0007063": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Mechanical and Mechatronic Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-11-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Webb School of Engineering at High Point University is seeking part-time Adjunct Instructors in Mechanical and Mechatronic Engineering. We are looking to fill sections of Mechanical, Mechatronic and General Engineering courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. QUALIFICATIONS: Education: An earned doctorate in engineering or closely related discipline is preferred. A master’s degree will be considered provided a minimum of 18 graduate credits in the discipline have been earned. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred. Experience in robotics, engineering design, or engineering graphics is a plus. Industry or related teaching experience is a plus. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Successfully teach introductory engineering courses at the collegiate level Must answer student emails promptly.  Must provide times to meet with students to facilitate learning as needed. High Point University is a God, family, and country school. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  To Apply: All applicants must submit the following: A letter of interest addressing the required qualifications and responsibilities A current CV with complete professional and academic history An unofficial transcript of your highest degree awarded Statement of teaching philosophy Names and contact information for three professional recommendations  All application materials must be uploaded as one file/attachment with resume/CV. Please refer questions to: Dr. Michael Oudshoorn, Dean of Engineering, at moudshoo@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Business-Communications_R0004160": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Business Communications",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-11-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Business Communications. We are looking to fill sections of Business Communications courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Ms. Lillian Watson, Director of the Business Communications Program at lwatson@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: A master’s degree in business administration, communication, OR a master’s degree plus commensurate experience in the teaching discipline will be considered. Upload an unofficial copy of your graduate transcript(s).  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). Be sure commensurate experience/training is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches Business Communications at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Business-Law_R0006977": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Business Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-10-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Business Law. We are looking to fill sections of Business Law courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Brad Venable, Chair of the Management Department at bvenable@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education : Juris Doctor from an ABA-approved law school Exemplary academic record Demonstrated interest in teaching and student mentorship and in creating an inspiring, welcoming, and dynamic learning environment for all students Upload an unofficial copy of your graduate transcript(s).  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). Be sure commensurate experience/training is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Preferred Qualifications: Relevant experience in the practice of law or in a related professional field Successful completion of the bar exam in at least one U.S. state Record of scholarly publications and presentations that contribute to the improvement of the law, legal education, and/or the legal profession Active engagement in professional organizations, such as discipline-specific organizations and bar associations Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches Business Law at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Entrepreneurship_R0004128": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-09-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe David S. Congdon School of Entrepreneurship at High Point University is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Entrepreneurship. We are looking to fill sections of Entrepreneurship courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Kathryn Elliott, Chair of the Department of Entrepreneurship at kelliott@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: Ph.D. in the teaching discipline preferred; a master’s degree and/or appropriate professional experience in the teaching discipline will be considered. Upload an unofficial copy of your Ph.D. and/or a master’s transcript.  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  This will be used to verify you have at least 18 graduate semester hours in Entrepreneurship. Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). If you have less than 18 hours, we will consider your commensurate experience/training.  Be sure this is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches Entrepreneurship at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Mathematical-Sciences_R0004370": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Mathematical Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-08-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nHigh Point University invites applications for multiple adjunct positions available in the Department of Mathematical Sciences in the Webb School of Engineering. Responsibilities: • Teach undergraduate courses in mathematics, statistics, and data analytics for both majors and non-majors, as assigned. • Other responsibilities include helping students in assigned courses, using Starfish, and providing student accommodations when necessary, and familiarity with Blackboard. Qualifications: Minimum qualifications: MS in mathematics, applied mathematics, statistics, data analytics, actuarial science, or a closely related field by August 2024. Successful applicants will (i) demonstrate an ability to teach mathematics or statistics courses, both for majors and non-majors, (ii) present evidence of teaching excellence at the high school or undergraduate level. The successful applicants will also present evidence of being able to engage students in the classroom. Preferred qualifications: Experience using Blackboard or similar teaching platforms such as Canvas. Experience using MyMathLab, StatLab, or other appropriate software such as R. The Department is especially interested in applicants who bring various perspectives to the University, and in those who may be especially effective in mentoring students who are members of groups that have been historically under-represented in the discipline. Application Materials Required: Submit the following items online at this website to complete your application:  Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Statement (2-page limit) Two References Letters (One of the two must address teaching. Letters to be submitted by references to Dr. Jenny Sharpe at jsharpe1@highpoint.edu .) You may also submit your application in a single uploaded document at:  https://highpoint.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Highpoint-Faculty. For additional information regarding this position, contact Dr. Jenny Sharpe at jsharpe1@highpoint.edu . About HPU: At High Point University the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in  an inspiring environment with caring people. High Point University is a God, family and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas. Department of Mathematical Sciences High Point University One North University Parkway Couch Hall 365 High Point, NC 27268"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Business-Analytics_R0006774": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Business Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Economics Department of the Earl N. Phillips School of Business is searching for a part-time adjunct instructor to teach BUA-5050 (Business Analytics I). This course is taught online asynchronously. The length of the course is eight weeks. Qualifications:   Education:   Doctorate degree in business analytics , statistics, OR related fields.     Experience and Training :   Online t eaching experience at the graduate college level is highly preferred.    Ability to teach PowerBI .     Knowledge, Skills, Ability :   Excellent verbal and written communication and computer skills   Ability to multi-task and work cooperatively with others   Skill dealing with a diverse group of people   Ability to work with and teach using electronic records   Ability to teach remotely     ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   Teach one or more sections of BUA-505 0: Business Analytics I, a two-credit, half semester course Maintain good communication and rapport with students, assist them in the completion of PowerBI assignments, and grade in a timely ma n ner     For more information regarding this position, please contact  Dr. Daniel Hall at dhall@highpoint.edu .     High Point University is an Equal Opportunity Employer .       The position will be considered open until filled."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Biology_R0006343": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Biology",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-03-25\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Wanek School of Natural Sciences at High Point University is seeking part-time Adjunct Instructors in Biology. We are looking to fill sections of Biology courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of Adjuncts for future consideration. Education: A Ph.D. or equivalent in biology, environmental science or a related field is preferred."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Attending-Dentist--Open-Rank-Faculty-Clinician--Primary-Care---Non-tenure-track_R0005449": {
      "title": "Attending Dentist, Open Rank Faculty Clinician (Primary Care), Non-tenure track",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-03-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description Summary High Point University Health, LLC and affiliated Oral Health Network is a non-for-profit oral health system that is part of the Workman School of Dental Medicine (WSDM), with a mission of putting those who need our care at the center of everything we do. The Attending Dentist, Faculty Clinician (Primary Care) is a full-time clinical position with a primary location in one of the OHN sites (HUB, primary oral health), all within one hour from High Point, NC. The HUB locations will provide multi-specialty and advanced complex care, the primary oral health sites will provide general dental services and affiliate hospitals will provide care to medically complex patients, all ensuring that the most complex of our patients' needs can be addressed within the OHN. This position will provide the Attending Dentist, Faculty Clinician (Primary Care) with the ability to grow, provide team-based patient care and education, in an authentic healthcare setting. The attending clinician will be able to connect to peers across the network and external healthcare partners via electronic health records (EPIC) and quality improvement using artificial intelligence (AI), under the guidance of the OHN Clinician Council and the office of the Chief Clinical Officer/Assistant Dean of WSDM. Attending clinicians are appointed as non-tenure, clinician-track faculty (Assistant/Associate/Professor) with duties in the High Point University Oral Health Network (OHN) and Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which includes the pre-doctoral Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) and post-doctoral programs. Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. QUALIFICATIONS: Education DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent), active dental licensure in the state of North Carolina Experience and Training 5 years of experience in clinical practice of dentistry is preferred, but not required. Experience in private practice is preferred, but not required. Experience in dental education is preferred, but not required. Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Robust verbal and written communication skills Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU WSDM’s core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Clinical documentation, diagnosis, and treatment planning using electronic health records (EHR) such as EPIC systems. Travel to OHN (oral health network) sites Adaptability Coachability Integrity and innovation Trustworthy ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   Patient care Provides comprehensive and emergency dental care to patients seen in the HPU Oral Health Network (OHN) Demonstrates the highest level of professionalism, ethics, and empathy toward patients Documents patient history, examination findings, diagnosis, treatment planning utilizing electronic health record (EPIC) Comfort with utilizing or adapting to digital technologies such as intraoral scanning, photography, 3d printing, CAD-CAM, and imaging. Covers for other OHN providers, as needed. Education Involved in the Clinician Council for quality improvement, best-practices, and material, equipment, and supplies. Serves as an attending clinical faculty for DMD and/or AEGD residents. Involved in pre-clinical and clinical curriculum design Provides continuing education courses in HPU WSDM as a content matter expert. Serves as a clinician role model for learners and be able to thrive in a start-up education model. Bridges connections with community initiatives that align with the values of High Point University. ACCOUNTABILITY: Report to Chief Clinical Officer (CCO), Dean Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews are conducted along with an annual assessment by the CCO. These reviews include input from the faculty and students. SALARY AND BENEFITS: Eligible candidates may meet criteria for Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) High Point University benefit and perks (employer matched 401K plan, vision, dental, health, tuition waiver for child, disability insurance, life insurance, CE and more. Base salary commensurate with experience and rank. OHN Incentive based on patient care thresholds. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Ali Muhammad Shazib, Dean, Workman School of Dental Medicine at mshazib@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--General-Dentistry_R0006261": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, General Dentistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-03-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThis is a part-time, adjunct faculty appointment with duties in the High Point University Workman School of Dental (WSDM), which delivers the Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) degree as well as a certificate in Advanced Education in General Dentistry (AEGD). Professional rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s level of experience and qualifications at time of hire. QUALIFICATIONS: Education DDS or DMD degree (or foreign equivalent), active full dental licensure in the state of North Carolina Experience and Training 30 years of experience in clinical practice of dentistry Preceptorship in a DMD or DDS program is preferred Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Robust verbal and written communication skills Exceptional receptiveness and approachability Poised and professional in representation of HPU WSDM Receptive to feedback, performance improvement, and continuous coaching Knowledge of HPU SDMOH’s core values and mission Strong ability to articulate operational and analytical data Clinical documentation, diagnosis, and treatment planning using electronic health records (EHR) such as EPIC systems. Travel to oral health network sites ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   The candidate selected for this position will perform all duties directed by the Dean of the WSDM: Pre-Doctoral Simulation Clinics Oversight, monitoring, and assessment of pre-clinical simulation lab performance, including operative and periodontal skills. Faculty will attend pre-clinical calibration in order to teach and assess students in the clinical skills coursework delivered in the first two years of the DMD curriculum. Case Presentation Faculty will have the opportunity to deliver case and problem-based learning as part of the first three years of the DMD curriculum. Clinical Preceptorship Faculty may be called upon, with proper notice and mutual agreement, by the Dean to provide coverage for DMD or AEGD learners in HPU Health practices. ACCOUNTABILITY: Dean Evaluation: Ongoing performance reviews is conducted along with an annual assessment by the Dean and includes input from the faculty and students. For more information regarding this position, please contact Jeffrey Lewallen, Operations Manager, Executive Leadership Team at jlewall1@highpoint.edu ."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--English_R0006173-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, English",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-01-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe High Point University Department of English is seeking to hire part-time instructors to teach first-year writing (FYW). The FYW curriculum is designed to engage students in active learning, a variety of research types, reflection, and a multimodal project. Applicants must have at least a Master’s Degree in English or related field and at least one year experience teaching FYW. To apply, create an account through the HPU Career Center website and submit a CV, brief cover letter, and a selection of teaching materials that may include any of the following: a past or current FYW syllabus, an assignment sequence, sample of student writing and instructor feedback, teaching philosophy, and/or teaching evaluations. For more information regarding this position please contact Dr. Bryan Vescio, Chair and Professor of English at bvescio@highpoint.edu."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Medical-Sciences_R0004069-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Medical Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-01-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Doctor of Medical Science Program within the Department of Medical Sciences at High Point University is seeking an Adjunct Instructor to serve as a Course Director. Course assignments commensurate with individual candidate experience, content expertise and program need. Assignments may include any of the following: EBM in Medical Sciences • EBM Principals – Cardiology – 3 cr. • EBM Principals – Gastroenterology & Nutrition – 3 cr. • EBM Principals – Pulmonology – 3 cr. • EBM Principals – Neurology – 3 cr. • EBM Principals – Musculoskeletal – 3 cr. • EBM Principals – Endocrinology – 3 cr. Healthcare Leadership • Self-Leadership Theory and Practice – 3 cr. • Healthcare Diversity, Equity and Inclusion – 3 cr. Patient Safety • Quality and Patient Safety – 2 cr. • Legal and Ethical Considerations in Healthcare – 2 cr. Research Methods • Medical Writing – 3 cr. • Statistics and Data Analysis in Healthcare – 3 cr. Health Professions Educator Concentration • Principles of Adult Learning – 3 cr. • Curricular Theory and Practice – 3 cr. • Program Assessment and Evaluation – 3 cr. • Online Teaching Theory and Practice – 3 cr. Health Professions Administration Concentration • Principles of Business and Strategic Planning – 3 cr. • Health Care Finance – 3 cr. • Operations Management – 3 cr. • Healthcare Information Technology – 3 cr. Courses within the DMS program are offered in 6-week sessions. Each adjunct faculty member will be assigned one course that will be offered annually in one of the following 6-week sessions: • Fall Semester: Session A, Session B • Spring Semester: Session A, Session B • Summer Semester: Session A, Session B Qualifications and Requirements: It is strongly preferred that DMS Adjunct Faculty have a doctorate degree and have the requisite knowledge and skills to teach in the program effectively.  Current NCCPA certification if a PA; current specialty board if a MD/DO.  Strong preference will be given to candidates with experience in teaching medical learners and familiarity with online learning.  A proven history in PA leadership, scholarship, and advocacy desired. Candidates located in remote locations to High Point, North Carolina will be considered. Key Responsibilities: Course content would need to be developed and uploaded into the Blackboard Ultra learning management system before the start of the 6-week course (session).    Course content/activities includes: Recorded lectures, Meaningful application activities or facilitation of thoughtful discussions via discussion boards, Interaction with students during the six weeks, Grading or evaluating student work/assignments, with grades submitted immediately after the end of the session.  It is expected that DMS adjunct faculty: Maintains effective assessment strategies for course and curriculum improvement. Fosters curricular and instructional approaches that recognize differences in individual learning, encourage problem-solving, and facilitate the acquisition of competencies and skills in the most efficient and effective manner possible. Ensures course specific student learning outcomes are achieved and incorporated from the program provided syllabus template through best educational practices in teaching and mentoring. Resources must either be provided or obtainable on-line through the university library system DMS students should not be required to purchase books for the course; however, the reading materials and topics that meet the learning objectives are up to the individual course instructor. The program roughly estimates 6 hours of time per week per course for students in the DMS program.  Recordings, activities, readings, and assignments should be geared to meet program defined learning outcomes using these “guiderails”.  Application review begins immediately and will continue until positions are filled. Candidates must successfully pass a background check that is satisfactory to the University. Applicants should upload a single PDF document including a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, summaries of teaching philosophy and teaching experience, transcripts, and the names and contact information of three professional references under the Resume / Cover Letter attachment section. For more information, please contact Dr. Linda Sekhon, Founding Chair of the Department of Medical Sciences and Professor of Medical Sciences and Professor of Physician Assistant Studies at lsekhon@highpoint.edu . General Information: The Department of Medical Sciences is housed in the Congdon School of Health Sciences.  Through excellence in teaching, scholarship, evidence-based clinical practice and community engagement, the Congdon School of Health Sciences advances patient-centered care across the lifespan by educating and preparing exceptional scholars and compassionate healthcare professionals who are dedicated to life-long learning and an inter-professional approach to achieving optimal outcomes.  At High Point University, every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people. High Point University is a God, family and country school.  High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas.  High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information or veteran status and other legally protected statuses.  The University encourages all applicants to apply. High Point University is an equal opportunity employer"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Faculty_R0002409": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Department of Interior Design and Home Furnishings",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-01-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Department of Interior Design and Home Furnishings is housed in the dynamic School of Art and Design at High Point University. The department is expanding and requires the addition of a new adjunct instructor to help us deliver an innovative, rigorous Bachelor of Science in Interior Design degree. The department also offers a minor in Visual Merchandising Design, and students greatly benefit from the school’s relationship with the High Point Market, the largest furniture market in the world. The department houses a tech lab and a Center for Innovation maker-space. We are committed to integrating technology with creativity, and we are looking to add enthusiastic, energetic faculty to help us realize our vision. High Point University is an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. For any questions related to the position, please contact Dr. Jane Nichols, Chair and Associate Professor at jnichols@highpoint.edu Adjunct professor position, to begin in January, 2022. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Terminal degree in interior design, architecture, or related discipline At least one degree must be in interior design or architecture Some experience teaching at the college/university level Be a good communicator, collaborator and team player who can thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced, extraordinary environment QUALIFICATIONS PREFERRED BUT NOT REQUIRED: PhD in relevant discipline RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach undergraduate lecture courses in interior design"
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Management_R0004129": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-01-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business at High Point University is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Management. We are looking to fill sections of Management courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Dave Tofanelli, Chair of the Department of Management and Entrepreneurship at dtofanel@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: Ph.D. in the teaching discipline preferred; a master’s degree and/or appropriate professional experience in the teaching discipline will be considered. Upload an unofficial copy of your Ph.D. and/or a master’s transcript.  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  This will be used to verify you have at least 18 graduate semester hours in Management. Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). If you have less than 18 hours, we will consider your commensurate experience/training.  Be sure this is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches Management at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas.  High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, and other legally protected statuses.  The University encourages all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Economics_R0004130": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Economics",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-01-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business at High Point University is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Economics. We are looking to fill sections of Economics courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Jerry Fox, Chair of the Department of Economics at jfox@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: Ph.D. in the teaching discipline preferred; a master’s degree and/or appropriate professional experience in the teaching discipline will be considered. Upload an unofficial copy of your Ph.D. and/or a master’s transcript.  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  This will be used to verify you have at least 18 graduate semester hours in Economics. Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). If you have less than 18 hours, we will consider your commensurate experience/training.  Be sure this is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches Economics at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas.  High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, and other legally protected statuses.  The University encourages all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Excel_R0004159": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Excel",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-01-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Phillips School of Business is seeking Adjunct Instructors, part-time in Excel. We are looking to fill sections of Excel courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. For more information regarding this position, please contact Dr. Jerry Fox, Chair of the Department of Economics at jfox@highpoint.edu. Qualifications and Application Materials Required: Education: A master’s degree plus commensurate experience in teaching Excel and/or data analysis software will be considered. Upload an unofficial copy of your graduate transcript(s).  Upon decision to hire, you will be expected to mail an official transcript.  Any graduate degree earned outside the U.S. will require a degree equivalency review (i.e., by World Education Services www.wes.org ). Be sure commensurate experience/training is clearly stated on your CV or resume, and list references who can testify to your experience/training. Experience/Training: Collegiate teaching experience is preferred, but not required. Upload a copy of your CV or resume.  Essential Functions: Successfully teaches Excel at the collegiate level Accountability: Must answer student emails promptly and be willing to schedule occasional appointments to meet with students. At High Point University, the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family, and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B visas.  High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, and other legally protected statuses.  The University encourages all qualified individuals to apply."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Adjunct-Instructor--Electrical-and-Computer-Engineering_R0005645-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-01-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Webb School of Engineering at High Point University is seeking part-time Adjunct Instructors in Electrical and Computer Engineering. We are looking to fill sections of Electrical and Computer Engineering courses on an as-needed basis. Successful applicants will be assigned a section for the upcoming session or be placed into our pool of adjuncts for future consideration. Teaching responsibilities will include lectures and labs in a variety of areas of the discipline, with particular interest in power and controls. Other duties include promptly communicating with students, meeting with students as necessary to facilitate learning, and collecting assessment data necessary for the ABET accreditation process. QUALIFICATIONS: Education A minimum of a master’s degree in electrical or computer engineering, or a closely related field is required; a Ph.D. and college-level teaching experience are preferred. Relevant industrial experience is also regarded as desirable. Applications should include the following items, submitted as a single document: (i) a cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position, (ii) curriculum vitae, (iii) an unofficial transcript with the highest awarded degree, and (iv) names and contact information for three professional references. At least one reference should be able to address the applicant’s potential or experience in teaching. For additional information, please contact Dr. Claire L. McCullough, Chair and Professor, Electrical and Computer Engineering, at cmccullo@highpoint.edu . Apply online at https://highpoint.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Highpoint-Faculty . High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas for part time positions. High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information or veteran status and other legally protected statuses.  The University encourages all applicants to apply."
    },
    "https://highpoint.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/High-Point-University/Pro-Bono-Clinic-Fellow_R0005973": {
      "title": "Pro Bono Clinic Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-01-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe RAISE Fellow trains in a one-year accredited post-professional orthopaedic manual physical therapy fellowship. The position includes clinical care, teaching (lab instruction and clinical mentorship), and service expectations in the High Point University Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) degree program. The RAISE Fellowship participant will complete clinical practice in the HPU Pro Bono Physical Therapy and Departmental/TEAM Clinics. These clinics provide physical therapy care to a varied patient population. As part of the RAISE Fellowship training program, protected mentoring time (a minimum of 150 hours) will focus on skills related to orthopaedic manual therapy, complex patient management, health behavior screening, and communication/advocacy. As such, applicants should possess both excellent clinical reasoning and clinical teaching skills. Candidates will be expected to demonstrate sound judgment, professional etiquette, and exceptional problem-solving skills. In addition to a strong desire to collaborate and make an impact in the community, candidates must have excellent communication skills that will allow them to interact with various groups of people. If desired, the RAISE Fellow may develop a caseload of Spanish-language patients. Further, the ideal candidate should be hard working, be able to make autonomous decisions, and offer suggestions for quality improvement. The fellowship program (see http://www.highpoint.edu/physicaltherapy/pbcfellow/) is dedicated to developing the expert clinician scientist. Upon successful completion of this program, the graduating RAISE fellow will ideally be a physical therapist who is capable of evaluating and managing a complex patient population via interventions using innovative technology, integrating the neuroscience of pain, highly skilled manual therapy techniques, and advanced communication styles. The graduating fellow will also have the opportunity to develop expertise in their desired specialty area, which can include individual and/or community health initiatives, professional advocacy, teaching, and/or research. QUALIFICATIONS: Education DPT degree (required) Experience and Training Current physical therapy license and/or eligible for licensure in the state of North Carolina (required) 1-3 years of clinical experience ( preferred- but new graduates will be considered) APTA Member (preferred) APTA certified clinical instructor (preferred) Experience working with various populations (preferred) Knowledge, Skills, Ability: Strong communication and interpersonal skills (required) Values teamwork, collaboration, self-awareness, and humility (required) Bilingual (preferred) ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS :   Contributes to the mission, vision, goals, and objectives of the Department, School, and University Provides excellent patient care Completes documentation in an accurate & timely manner Completes didactic coursework and successful matriculation through the fellowship training program Meets departmental standards related to clinical and classroom teaching Completes clinical/or laboratory research in an ethical manner Any questions related to this position should be sent to Dr. Alicia Emerson, Assistant Professor, Physical Therapy at aemerson1@highpoint.edu . At High Point University the faculty and staff are devoted to ensuring every student receives an extraordinary education in an inspiring environment with caring people.  High Point University is a God, family and country school. High Point University does not sponsor H1-B Visas.  High Point University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, genetic information or veteran status and other legally protected statuses.  The University encourages all applicants to apply."
    }
  },
